{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5","id":1398959,"title":"Thinking about M5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-26T00:34:04-07:00","id":1398959,"title":"Thinking about M5","content":"It's a long way off, if we ever do see it, but when we do, I think we should expect some big changes. I don't expect all of them to be popular.<br /> <br /> First of all, I think the traditions need an update. Trads like the Verbenae and the Euthanatos need to drop some of the artistic license that has been heaped on them. V5 responded to this, I think, to just let the Ravnos fade out of the picture. I would rather see this unnecessary baggage fade away and leave a more culturally sensitive traditions in their wake.<br /> <br /> In M20 Brucato opened up the favored spheres options for the traditions. While I like neat and orderly systems where everyone has a place, I think for a group as diverse as the traditions to stay in neat little categories is pretty unrealistic, which is why he did it. The fact that the Disparate Alliance is even a thing is kind of a failure of the Traditions, when they insisted on shoving all of the &quot;crafts&quot; into preexisting Traditions. I would like to see an M5 where either the Disparate Alliance has been brought into the fold of the Traditions, or there is some kind of diplomatic process ongoing between the Disparates and Traditions, as they are both really fighting for the same thing. Perhaps even with the Dreamspeakers/Kha'vadi &quot;crossing the table&quot; so to speak. <br /> <br /> That said, I think one issue Mage is going to have to grapple with is that when you look at the Traditions and Disparates, you see the religions of the world laid out before you almost like character classes. On one hand this might lead players to investigate belief systems and cultures that are outside their normal experience, which is ultimately a good thing. On the other, the writers have to be very careful in how these things are presented, and that isn't always easy. Not all of them have been handled well in the past, and changing them while keeping the fans happy is a difficult balance. They had several missteps in how they rolled out V5, and unless they can get their house in order, Mage proves to be a virtual minefield.<br /> <br /> As for the Technocracy, I think the conflict of magic vs. technology is largely over. I think the real question with technology is one of ethics. Information is being gathered on people at an unprecedented scale. Governments are spying on their own citizens. Fascism is on the rise, and people are beginning to question capitalism. Global warming is becoming even more threatening every year. I think it is on these questions that the Technocracy is going to have to declare where they stand. I don't think it is reasonable to expect that the Technocracy will be a monolith in that regard. I don't read the technocracy books much to see how they are presented lately but I think there should be a significant portion of the technocracy that are really in it for the power. &quot;protecting the sleepers&quot; is starting to wear pretty thin and I think a number of technocrats are going to have to face up to that. I expect that a significant number of technocrats are going to push back against the new technocratic dictators, which will probably be a major source of struggle in M5.<br /> <br /> In terms of the spheres, I would expect a bit of a restructuring here. In V5, we saw the Disciplines transformed into trees: one character with Potence 3 is not necessarily going to be the same as another with Potence 3, depending on what abilities they chose. I think we might see similar in M5. One mage with Forces might do better with natural phenomena, like weather, fire, or temperature while another might do better with magnetism, radio waves, and lasers. A Spirit Mage might be able to summon and bind spirits, while another might do better at mediation. <br /> <br /> And/or we might see a unifying structure like the practices in Mage: The Awakening applied to the Spheres. Sometimes the spheres can feel a little haphazard (Entropy 5 lets you do entropic mind effects... without Mind?) and the Practices of Awakening do a lot to help to understand the spheres.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of us see the potential of the hunger dice system being adapted to paradox. I hope they give paradox plenty of teeth. I think the setting feels a little thin when mages get away with blatant effects with little repercussion. <br /> <br /> Mage has always had a bit of a cult following, and I think if they are interested in bringing M5 to life, they are going to want to make the game a lot more newbie friendly. I think it can be done, but I wonder how many Mage fans are going to stand for the changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T01:26:20-07:00","id":1398969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5#post1398959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a long way off, if we ever do see it, but when we do, I think we should expect some big changes. I don't expect all of them to be popular.<br /> <br /> In M20 Brucato opened up the favored spheres options for the traditions. While I like neat and orderly systems where everyone has a place, I think for a group as diverse as the traditions to stay in neat little categories is pretty unrealistic, which is why he did it. </div> </div> </div> </div>This has been a part of Mage since the Revised Tradition books or even before, I think...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T02:06:29-07:00","id":1398980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1398969#post1398969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This has been a part of Mage since the Revised Tradition books or even before, I think...</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of. In Revised, each tradition had one official favored sphere, and different traditions described subfactions that replaced the favored sphere with another one. Often these subfactions were crafts that had been absorbed into the Tradition, since by Revised fiction, the crafts had all but been wiped out. (i.e. The Order of Hermes' favored sphere was Forces, but if I chose House Fortunae, I could choose Entropy as my favored sphere.)<br /> <br /> M20 broke with that and just gave some traditions multiple options when selecting favored sphere, no strings attached. M20 also favored giving many of the former crafts their own identities again in the Disparate Alliance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","user":"Froggy711","date":". 06-26-2020, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T02:33:33-07:00","id":1398985,"title":"","content":"Yes, you are right. Kind of, but the seed was already there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T02:43:46-07:00","id":1398986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1398985#post1398985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you are right. Kind of, but the seed was already there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess what I was trying to say is that we will probably see a continuation of this trend. The &quot;9 seat&quot; system of the Traditions may completely go out the window. We may see the Disparate Alliance and the Traditions come under the same umbrella, partially or in whole, or even see Traditions leave and join the Disparates. I think how this plays out will depend a lot on how these groups can be handled while keeping an eye on cultural sensitivity, and still keeping the fans happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T03:18:57-07:00","id":1398993,"title":"","content":"Aside for a need for brevity and a streamlining of the magic system there are a few things I'd <i>love</i> to see:<br /> <br /> 1: Is that I'd love to see an idea in the storyteller's handbook followed up on as the foundation for the traditions in m5, continuing where revised left off: that the fall of the Archmagi was actually a <i>good</i> thing, it was an idea that changed my entire perspective on revised; the idea that a bunch of powerful obsolete old folks had decided to retreat from the world and spend their time politicking and trying to win a fight they lost in the renaissance in some far-flung spirit world wasn't helping the world or the tradition's cause, and that without being tied down by people with ancient grudges and little respect for the modern era the mages actually have an opportunity to <i>change</i> things and are in a better position to band together and have a greater tolerance for eachother than ever before. Take revised's focus and change the presentation to an <i>optimistic </i>one, being about rediscovering lost ancient lore (perhaps have that as a prerequisite for seekings required to actually up both gnosis and spheres, you'd actually have to earn something about magic), uniting the scattered traditions and actually making headway into becoming apart of consensus. For a game about the ascension war, it'd be nice if that actually mattered, keep revised's street-level focus and be about what new wonder or terror is behind the curtain.<br /> <br /> 2: Trigger a technocracy schism, as a group the technocracy has always been inconsistently either Orwellian Illuminati seeking to control the world and suppress humanity and the protectors of humanity from magic boldly exploring the boundaries of Science! and they've never quite been willing to commit more fully to either one, and instead letting the storyteller decide, not an inherently bad idea but it does make them a bit inconsistent narratively. However, late in revised it was heavily implied that the higher orders of the Technocracy had fallen to the nephandi and become a force that was actively crippling mankind's ability to awaken. Build on that idea, have a large number of lower-ranking members and void engineers defect to form their own order, taking back their original name of the Order of Reason to distinguish themselves and refocus on being a force of innovation for humanity and have them band together with the new council, allowing you to distinguish between playable technocracy and the technocracy as an antagonist faction (as well as lose that subtle 'modern technology is bad' vibe Mage never quite lost)<br /> <br /> Let that be the status quo focused on in the text, a united front of innovaters and philosophers of all kind fighting against a stagnant and tyrannical force. If the WoD5 era is about going back to thematic basics with a revised system than let M5 be about going back to 1st editions street level conspiracies within mysteries, let it be a game about discovering magic, more than just knowing it. Let the bleakness of the revised era give way to a more fun game about fighting for humanity with reality itself on the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T04:35:16-07:00","id":1399016,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting, I think, to see Brucato's <b>Mage Made Easy</b> used as a blueprint for M5:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Start Simple, then add more: have the overall plan be for the M5 core book to be geared toward a style of play that's intimate, immediate, and personal, discarding metaplot and emphasizing arcane approaches instead of mystical societies, while sticking mostly to the mortal realm. But have the first wave of supplements dive into the elements of Mage that the above only briefly sketches or leaves out entirely. For instance, the first supplement after the core book could be \u201cAscension War\u201d; and <i>this</i> book, not the core book, would introduce the Traditions, Technocracy, and Disparates, and the history and current affairs of the struggle in which they're engaged. Another early supplement would be a new edition of the Book of Worlds, which would facilitate games that delve deeply into Mage's otherworlds. And so on. <br /> <br /> \u2022 M5 magic would <i>start</i> with Focus, followed by Common Magickal Effects, and only <i>then</i> get into the Spheres. Consider listing a half-dozen or so Common Magickal Effects for each Practice, so a player has some idea at a glance not only of how the Practitioners Magick works, but also what it does. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Replace the Coincidental/Vulgar divide with a Subtle/Uncanny/Extreme split, and replace Paradox with Resonance and/or Echoes; or replace the Backlash mechanics with something potentially as simple as \u201ca five-point Backlash manifests as a five-success Effect that your character could perform (i.e., conforming to his Focus and Spheres), but chosen and directed by the Storyteller instead of the player.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T04:52:42-07:00","id":1399021,"title":"","content":"I have not read Mage Made Easy, but his M20 work has certainly made me a fan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T04:58:19-07:00","id":1399024,"title":"","content":"What I would like to see is like someone commented before a split in the technocracy and the traditions, with that split creating a new organization formed by the sons of the ether, the virtual adepts, nuavalon, the void engineers, and maybe someone else. They would act as a counterpoint to the technocracy, while the technocracy becomes a literal Illuminati like conspiracy obsessed with absolute control no matte r what. The traditions would absorb some of the disparate alliance organizations and become sort of guardians of the mythical and mystical, not with the intention of bringing a new dark age, but to guard the loss of knowledge and show humanity the power they have within themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T05:38:03-07:00","id":1399035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1399024#post1399024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I would like to see is like someone commented before a split in the technocracy and the traditions, with that split creating a new organization formed by the sons of the ether, the virtual adepts, nuavalon, the void engineers, and maybe someone else. They would act as a counterpoint to the technocracy, while the technocracy becomes a literal Illuminati like conspiracy obsessed with absolute control no matte r what. The traditions would absorb some of the disparate alliance organizations and become sort of guardians of the mythical and mystical, not with the intention of bringing a new dark age, but to guard the loss of knowledge and show humanity the power they have within themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I posted this factional setup a while back:<br /> <br /> ~~~~<br /> <br /> THE TRADITIONS<br /> -Led by the New Horizon Council based in New Zealand, they seek to keep magic and mysticism alive in the modern world, generally fine with modern society and technology.<br /> -Order of Hermes,<br /> -Euthanatos/Chakravanti<br /> -Solificati/Children of Knowledge<br /> -Ahl-i-Batin<br /> -Verbena<br /> -Dreamspeakers/Kha'vadi<br /> -Celestial Chorus<br /> -Akashayana<br /> -CoX/Sahajiya<br /> <br /> THE NEW ORDER OF REASON<br /> -Seek to purge the corrupted leaders of the Technocracy to establish a safe, stable reality and lead mankind into a technological utopia.<br /> -IBM (International Brotherhood of Mechanicians), ItX as presented in Revised<br /> -Virtual Adepts<br /> -Society of Ether (Highly tense with the others apart from the Adepts, it's unclear if they'll stick on after Threat Null is dealt with)<br /> -Revised Syndicate<br /> -Revised Progenitors (One of the smallest conventions of the NOR, large numbers stayed with the Technocracy)<br /> -Lightkeepers (Revised NWO, also rather small)<br /> -Void Engineers<br /> <br /> TECHNOCRATIC UNION<br /> -Corrupted by Threat Null, the leadership have become as ruthless and totalitarian as they were back in the early 90s. These co-opted elements must be taken down before they break down the Gauntlet and allow Threat Null to openly invade Earth ...<br /> <br /> THE DISPARATE ALLIANCE<br /> -A grab-bag of insular crafts allied for self-defense who try to keep their idiosyncratic cultural forms of magic alive in the modern day, and reject the idea of the Traditions that all mages essentially do the same thing.<br /> <br /> ROGUE COUNCIL<br /> -Fanatical traditionalists led by spiritised Tradition masters and archmasters in the Umbra, a mix of old-school Ascension warriors who never stopped fighting for various personal reasons and younger mages who have romanticised the conflicts of the past. The strawman version of the Traditions, these are radicals who reject the New Horizon Council and want to bring modern civilisation down so they can party like it's 1399.<br /> <br /> NEPHANDI AND MARAUDERS<br /> -You know the drill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 06-26-2020, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T07:13:45-07:00","id":1399057,"title":"","content":"I'd prefer a setting update that at once both more modest and more radical than that. <br /> <br /> More modest: the Traditions get renamed as per M20's New Horizon Council. The Technocracy has reorganized, and Navalon had jumped ship. And the Disparate Alliance has \u201cgone public\u201d (to the extent that any secret society can go public). <br /> <br /> More radical: the default protagonists of the game are what used to be called Orphans \u2014 though as with M20, they've got all the diversity of the magical organizations of the earlier editions, and then some. <br /> <br /> The more aggressive Technocracy is pretty much required, considering that it is apparently behind V5's Second Inquisition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T11:42:55-07:00","id":1399106,"title":"","content":"-The Avatar storm has chilled out<br /> -Mages have become more interested in political ideology, and there is some small infighting with that, but there's nothing huge to shake up how things are going. Perhaps they see ascension as something that might need to happen soon. The Nephandi are everywhere; the left, the right, big government and small. <i>Don't make the same mistake as vampire</i>. <br /> -The M20 alternative names never happened. The disparates remain seperate. <br /> <br /> <br /> I actually think they can't do a mage. Given how they've treated magic in vampire, it seems a bit much to ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T14:21:30-07:00","id":1399136,"title":"","content":"I'm the opposite. I hope they keep the new tradition names and the Disparate Alliance. For me, both of these changes feel like a logical progression within the setting. Assuming the Avatar Storm did happen, and the Archmages are gone, then it would be the younger mages, with more modern ideas, who are in charge of the Traditions. The new names are a nice way to underscore that there are new people in charge, with different values, who want to be perceived differently than their predecessors.<br /> <br /> And honestly, I've always loved the idea of the Disparate Alliance. The Traditions aren't the answer for everyone and it makes sense to me that the Crafts would both want to protect themselves, but also not want to get involved in the Traditions' particular brand of politics. I'd really like to see some long term ramifications of the sudden emergence of a new group amidst the long time Ascension War stalwarts.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I'm not really sure what I'd want to see. I think maybe I'd like to see more focus on the individual Traditions, Conventions, and Crafts as their own entities, beyond their roles as part of the Traditions/Technocracy/Alliance. Like what kind of secret goals, or alliances, or rivalries do they have between one another? What are the Janissaries or the House Helekars of this new generation? That kind of thing.<br /> <br /> ETA: Mostly, I'd really like to see more emphasis on conflict that isn't just Nephandi manipulation. I like the Nephandi, as villains, but I sometimes think the setting relies a bit too much on them, when the Traditions and Conventions, and probably the Crafts too, are full of plenty of jerks who can make trouble for their own reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 06-26-2020, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T21:30:58-07:00","id":1399202,"title":"","content":"IBM (International Brotherhood of Mechanicians) is a cool alternative to It X.<br /> <br /> I've been tinkering around with the idea of naming a group in the Technocracy that just does chemistry/physics stuff but I'm lacking a name....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T22:05:27-07:00","id":1399206,"title":"","content":"I'm also a big fan of both the new names for the Traditions and the Disparate Alliance (with the one sticking point that Orphans should be more clearly divided from them) for much of the reasons said above - both to show the progression of time and in some cases to provide more accurate names or to counter some of the ambiences that have sprouted up amongst the traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T22:05:51-07:00","id":1399207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1399136#post1399136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ETA: Mostly, I'd really like to see more emphasis on conflict that isn't just Nephandi manipulation. I like the Nephandi, as villains, but I sometimes think the setting relies a bit too much on them, when the Traditions and Conventions, and probably the Crafts too, are full of plenty of jerks who can make trouble for their own reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>When it comes to the Nephandi, less is more. Not every crooked mage has a steeple-fingered nephandus behind them, when there are human foibles like, oh, greed or hubris to screw everyone over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T10:29:11-07:00","id":1399314,"title":"","content":"You guys are progressive (no?) I don't think Hubris filled mages, in the World of Darkness, who are devided into houses and such within traditions, would aprove of all the names given in m20. some? sure; but not others. The traditions arent soley stocked with &quot;progressives&quot; like the m20 writing staff. There are many conservatives, many people who are cynical towards the idea of returning to an 'old' name of a culture the tradition has moved away from and of which is foreign to them. In a democracy, most of m20's name changes would not have gone through. perhaps they would move towards a different name, perhaps they would stick. it's been a bit since i last read m20. i thought it rather telling that most of the rest if the book used the old names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T11:19:27-07:00","id":1399323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1399314#post1399314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys are progressive (no?)</div> </div> </div> </div> no, not in my case. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1399314#post1399314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Hubris filled mages, in the World of Darkness, who are divided into houses and such within traditions, would aprove of all the names given in m20. some? sure; but not others. The traditions arent soley stocked with &amp;quot;progressives&amp;quot; like the m20 writing staff. There are many conservatives, many people who are cynical towards the idea of returning to an 'old' name of a culture the tradition has moved away from and of which is foreign to them. In a democracy, most of m20's name changes would not have gone through. perhaps they would move towards a different name, perhaps they would stick. it's been a bit since i last read m20. i thought it rather telling that most of the rest if the book used the old names.</div> </div> </div> </div> Euthanatos \u2192 Chakravanti is a new name reverting to an old name. So is Dreamspeakers\u2192Kha'vadi, and Cult of Ecstasy\u2192Sahajiya. <br /> <br /> Akashic Brotherhood\u2192Akashayana isn't; it's a shift from external name to internal name \u2014 that is, they've always called themselves Akashayana; now they're insisting that others call them that, too. <br /> <br /> Sons of Ether\u2192Society of Ether isn't a reversion to an older name, either. I'll grant that the impetus for this particular name change is progressive in nature; but it's not a name change that I, as a conservative, feel any interest in opposing. I rather like \u201cSociety of Ether\u201d, personally. <br /> <br /> Virtual Adepts\u2192Mercurial Elites: this is the only name-change that makes me go \u201cwhy?\u201d<br /> <br /> More generally, the typical conservative strikes me as not particularly having strong feelings about the names; for the most part, their reaction is most likely along the lines of \u201cI don't know why you're making such a fuss over the name; but there's no skin off my nose if you change it.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T11:37:26-07:00","id":1399333,"title":"","content":"As I said, I like the names because they show momentum within the Traditions, which reflects the fact that, due to the metaplot, the oldest and most powerful mages are gone. Now the Traditions are led by new, younger Mages, who have their own Hubris. And that Hubris may well take the form of wanting to reform their Traditions in their own image.<br /> <br /> Assuming M5 is like V5, then we are going to see metaplot progression. There's no reason to expect everything to revert to the 2nd Edition stasis, even if that's an option in Mage 20. This is an obvious way to demonstrate it.<br /> <br /> It's not like a storyteller HAS to use the new names though. If the Mages in your Chronicle aren't as innovative and progressive, you don't have to use the new names. But I hope they keep them, or incorporate other signs of forward momentum in their place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T11:37:45-07:00","id":1399334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1399314#post1399314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys are progressive (no?) I don't think Hubris filled mages, in the World of Darkness, who are devided into houses and such within traditions, would aprove of all the names given in m20. some? sure; but not others. The traditions arent soley stocked with &quot;progressives&quot; like the m20 writing staff. There are many conservatives, many people who are cynical towards the idea of returning to an 'old' name of a culture the tradition has moved away from and of which is foreign to them. In a democracy, most of m20's name changes would not have gone through. perhaps they would move towards a different name, perhaps they would stick. it's been a bit since i last read m20. i thought it rather telling that most of the rest if the book used the old names.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't speculate on people's politics, please. ESPECIALLY not developers. Just stick to the setting as presented.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T11:41:28-07:00","id":1399338,"title":"","content":"You've not met many then. They love names and statues and making things like an imagined past whilst dreading the future.... <br /> <br /> Euthanatos is one that bothers me. Just makes me think of predominantly white women who want to enshrine a minority as some nice, pure 'other' that's more in touch with nature. such pure people need to be kept away from the corruption of nasty modernity...<br /> <br /> It's bullshit. This return of modernized people to a traditional ancient sounding.... <br /> <br /> Virtual adepts do need an update, but that is clearly not the name for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T11:55:02-07:00","id":1399344,"title":"","content":"The Euthanatos's Wheel concept has had its origin in South Asian philosophy since the First Edition. The entire backstory with the Akashayana is based around the fact that they're both Asian Traditions that incorporate the concept of Reincarnation. Kali and the Thuggies have been used as thematic examples for a very long time, and Voormas is both East Asian, himself, and his art depictions are clearly inspired by Hindu religious art. The spokes of the wheel are called Chakra-Dharma in the first Tradition book. &quot;Jhor&quot; is not a Greek word.<br /> <br /> And like Akashayana, the Chakravanti name appears as early as the first Tradition book, so it's not actually a new idea.<br /> <br /> The Euthanatos name works as a subset for the specific Tradition members who use Greek or Celtic religious elements in their practice, but it makes much more sense, to me, for the very heavily South Asian inspired Tradition to have a name that reflects that.<br /> <br /> I'm certainly not saying anyone has to use the new name. But I think it makes sense. Especially when we consider how, in the game's metaplot, all the stuff with House Helekar and Voormas would have happened relatively recently, and perhaps would have inspired the Tradition to embrace a change of external image.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T12:59:43-07:00","id":1399357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1399338#post1399338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've not met many then. They love names and statues and making things like an imagined past whilst dreading the future.... <br /> <br /> Euthanatos is one that bothers me. Just makes me think of predominantly white women who want to enshrine a minority as some nice, pure 'other' that's more in touch with nature. such pure people need to be kept away from the corruption of nasty modernity...<br /> <br /> It's bullshit. This return of modernized people to a traditional ancient sounding.... <br /> <br /> Virtual adepts do need an update, but that is clearly not the name for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll let the first part slide, per CTPhipps' instructions. <br /> <br /> On the Euthanatoi/Chakravanti thing: the names for the Traditions first appeared in M1e, before they got fleshed out in their respective Tradition Books. When they <i>did</i> get fleshed out, they occasionally ended up being significantly different than the stereotypes of them that were embodied in their original descriptions. The Euthanatoi are a prime example of this: originally portrayed as death-mages and assassins, their expanded treatment has them as much more than that: death magic and assassination is what they're best known for because they're the only Tradition that's willing to do the dirty work that needs to be done; but it's only a small part of what they do. The shift from Euthanatos to Chakravanti is about recognizing that the Tradition is more about the wheel of fate than about death and killing; it's not about \u201ccleaning them up\u201d as it is about being more accurate. Of the three \u201creversion\u201d name changes, it's the one that bothers me the <i>least</i>. <br /> <br /> And I'm fine with \u201cVirtual Adepts\u201d; I don't think they need a rebranding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-05-2020, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T14:07:14-07:00","id":1399371,"title":"","content":"Yeah I probably could've wrote that first bit better. There's a spectrum of conservative, the more colourful ones outshine others.<br /> <br /> So with the Chakravanti thing.<br /> <br /> Fundamentally, on the most visible level of things, You should keep as much as you can in the language you speak. For the uninitiated, the least amount of loanwords you use, the better. &quot;we're the <i>Chakravanti</i>&quot; doesn't sell as well as, say, &quot;we're the Wheel&quot; or the Tapestry or the cycle, especially when you're the whitest Canadian the world has ever seen. Once people have taken the hook you can really get into Dharmas, but if you try too hard too soon you come off as a wanker who's trying to sound fancy and cultured and &quot;Culturally appropriating&quot;. You need a shiny, easily digestible name to attract people into the deep end of your philosophy. I really love the Samsara path of Paradox for Ravnos, and all it's Dharma stuff, but the draw of the name there is the Path of Paradox, which gives me some idea of what the path might be about. The other stuff just looks like noise until you invest in it. When you're trying to sell all the different traditions to players, you need them to have clean and easy names. Few people understand whichever particular indian language Chakravanti comes from and can't discern it's meaning due to this lack of knowledge (Euthanatoi draws from Euthanasia and Thanos so it's a lot more helpful for westerners)<br /> <br /> As for &quot;Virtual Adepts&quot;<br /> pffftt. how dated is this? Computer culture has evolved so far beyond this it's like calling Istambul Constantinople. It might work Ironically I guess. Internet loves irony.<br /> <br /> You should call them<i> Tech wizards</i>. It'll never fall out of fashion.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T15:08:35-07:00","id":1399400,"title":"","content":"I think the VA started calling themselves the Mercurial Elite in M20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T15:36:03-07:00","id":1399411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1399323#post1399323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Virtual Adepts\u2192Mercurial Elites: this is the only name-change that makes me go \u201cwhy?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does this strike me as their way of trying to annoy some of the Hermetics?<br /> Also, it'd be hilarious if they updated their name again to something even more random in M20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T15:43:36-07:00","id":1399415,"title":"","content":"The idea that the Virtual Adepts chose their new names specifically to annoy the Hermetics does more to sell me on the name than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 06-27-2020, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T18:01:58-07:00","id":1399443,"title":"","content":"'Mercurial Elite' is honestly the only M20 name update I'm not entirely sold on and that's just because it doesn't have quite the same ring to me it might have for others, but I talked about that in an old thread and that's really a just a matter of personal taste.<br /> <br /> As for the matter of 'Chalravanti', I don't think many traditions are in-setting much worried about how their name works for PR or recruitment. There more likely to actually want accurate names because this is magick and names have power. The greek elements are not the best representatives of the tradition and its philosophy as a whole, the Indian/Vedic elements are, thus 'Chakravanti' as their term; one which they've been using since first edition but that for the purpose of branding they've been called the 'Euthanatos' instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T08:54:53-07:00","id":1399603,"title":"","content":"But I don't think the Chak that aren't indian, who have celtic,greek or whatever philosophies, are going to be sold on the Indian name. That just sounds like 'those indians think they're better than us' talk. Settling for a cross-faith term makes everyone happy, changing a culturally exclusive name for another is just... not a reasonable move unless one group exploded in strength to supress the others (maybe in a couple decades the indians will do that) or its a move a complete outsider made in order to appear progressive... hmmm....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T09:16:04-07:00","id":1399605,"title":"","content":"Frankly, my biggest issue with the Tradition being renamed as the Chakravanti is that the largest faction within the Tradition is called\u2026 the Chakravanti. If the Tradition as a whole takes up that name, what does the Indian faction within it call themselves? <br /> <br /> Other than that, I don't see a problem with the Tradition as a whole taking on that name: as I mentioned, the Indian faction within the Tradition is the <i>largest</i> faction within the Tradition, and is likely to have the most say as to what the Tradition is going to call itself going forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T09:19:48-07:00","id":1399606,"title":"","content":"Why would the Chakravanti need to brand themselves in the first place? They're not a club thirsting for members, they're an ancient religious tradition with a very deep and involved philosophy. They have some Greek and Celtic members who have religious leanings toward chthonic deities and a similar practice, but they're relatively few and far between. The bulk of the Tradition has always been about the Wheel.<br /> <br /> The Chakravanti isn't any more or less a &quot;culturally exclusive&quot; name than the Euthanatos. It's Indian rather than Greek, which makes it a better representation of the Tradition's history as a whole. Besides, if they're looking for new members: there's a LOT of people in India, who already may have compatible philosophical leanings and a familiarity with the culture. They don't exactly need European or American recruits any more than the Akashayana do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T13:09:23-07:00","id":1399644,"title":"","content":"the thing about marketing isn't that you aren't trying to get people to join your organization, you're trying to sell your name as a respectable one because people want to do business with people they've heard of before. You aren't recruiting people with good branding, but you are influencing how people think of your organization and how much they're likely to do business with you. Say someone from the Order of hermes needs to hire a local mage to do something she can't do on her own; A bunch of Celts going by an Indian name doesn't appeal to most people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T13:33:01-07:00","id":1399651,"title":"","content":"I think you've lost me here. Are we talking about branding in an in character sense? Because I sincerely doubt the death mages who are focused on protecting and guiding the wheel care that much about how they're marketing to people who aren't their chosen students/apprentices. The Chakravanti/Euthanatos have never been the kind of Tradition that chases after potential members.<br /> <br /> If we're talking about out of character branding, then I'd imagine that the powers that be will be considering all of these factors. But generally speaking, most mage players are familiar enough with the properties to be able to choose what Tradition (or Convention or Craft) appeals to them regardless of the name. If players can get used to names like &quot;Tzimisce&quot;, I think they can figure out &quot;Chakravanti&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 06-28-2020, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T13:40:30-07:00","id":1399653,"title":"","content":"New editions let designers rename things so that things have what the designers feel are the best names for them. Sometimes that means bringing forward an alternate name from the lore to be the main name, and sometimes it means making up a new one. They may have a rationale in the fiction for the change, but we all know it\u2019s because they wanted to change the name of the thing and did. Arguing about the in-fiction rationale that they came up with after the fact doesn\u2019t really accomplish anything.<br /> <br /> Also, are we really pretending that English-speakers have an easier time with Greek than Sanskrit? I really don\u2019t believe that to be the case. They\u2019re both equally strange to Anglo eyes. My main thing with <i>chakravanti</i> is that I can\u2019t figure out the etymology of the second part (<i>chakra</i> is easy). I had always assumed it was a typo of <i>chakravarti</i>.<br /> <br /> In any case, I can hardly wait for M5 and will buy the shit out of it at the earliest opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 06-28-2020, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T15:08:34-07:00","id":1399681,"title":"","content":"No I mean... <br /> <br /> Lets say you want to offer your services for fun and profit to other mages that don't quite have the skills you do. <br /> You are a welsh mage of the Chakravanti tradition.<br /> <br /> Your magic stems from Celtic belief by the way. You got lumped in with the Chakravanti lot because of similarities. Since the Indian Chakravants can claim their magic older, and they've had the entire tradition change names, many people have began to assume that your magic is some kind of derivative. (At least with the Euthanatoi, you could blame the greek-roman connection and how that stuff conquered europe. India has had little impact on your celtic stuff to your knowledge) Maybe some scholar can point out that your tradition is a devolvment of the indian belief system, maybe it was an independent development, it doesn't matter. You are a proud welsh mage that practices a belief several-thousand years independent from india. <br /> <br /> If you used a welsh name, people would have to think about it and translate it within their heads and go 'oh, you're with that indian tradition' which hurts your all-important mage pride.<br /> If you said you're Chakravanti you would belittle your all-important beliefs and you'd get weird looks for being the whitest guy claiming to be indian. <br /> <br /> These options undermine your bargaining power. If there are two entropic mages offering services to others, one person seems all together, and the other person is a white welshman playing the indian, the former has an advantage. <br /> (Note: if you did things the other way around, India is enough of a bubble that it wouldn't matter what the europeans named the tradition) <br /> <br /> If you went with something culturally neutral (The circle, The tapestry, the Cycle) Then you don't have any identity issues regardless of you being Welsh, Greek or Bhurmese. You can move to any country and market your Magick to other mages who need it evenly. Your Welsh magic does not have the connotations of being a culturally appropriated Indian magic. <br /> <br /> No european mage would be happy with that connotation. It's not an issue of racism (It could be) it's that their magic works with their own, very old, cultural practices, and it's an attack on their very being to have their beliefs play second fiddle to a foreign one, even if it the big beats are similar, the details aren't, and mages go all in on details.<br /> <br /> Catholics and Protestants have a lot in common, and they were burning eachother a few hundred years ago. Today, If you started calling ardent protestants catholic, two groups would be at the least annoyed, and if you started calling them both jewish (Let's pretend there's no baggage to that, and it's just a matter of thinking all the Abrahamic religions should be named after their original faith) You'd be causing quite the frustration with three. <br /> While I'm sure some Indian Chakravanti would be absolutely delighted to impose their name on everyone in their tradition, a good few would sensible, and a good few would be loath that a welshman, with his beliefs that only match up to theirs from a shallow outside perspective, would be included in the Chakravanti label. Some people want a big brand, others want a selective brand. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's just not good, Ok? What would be wrong with an all-encompassing name that doesn't make anyone's beliefs secondary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T15:51:06-07:00","id":1399684,"title":"","content":"Alrighty so I think I get what you mean to say here.<br /> <br /> Going along with your example, I believe what you are describing is a very intentional quality of the traditions. The Council of Traditions is made up of broad umbrellas of loosely associated groups that do not all entirely agree despite the similarities of their beliefs. That tension goes back to the arrogance of the tradition founders and it's one of the big reasons why there is both so much tension within and between traditions but also between tradition and craft mages.<br /> <br /> The hypothetical welsh mage has a few options. They can accept membership in a tradition founded by Indian mages whose paradigm mos resembles his own or they can go another way. The Verbena provide a more closely associated culture but neither the terms and associated cultures of the Euthanoi or Chakravanti really suit his culture. So he must choose between being a fringe member of this tradition or refusing membership and joining/forming a gaelic craft that suits his paradigm.<br /> <br /> It facilitates the punk aspects of Mage as a gothic punk setting that one must choose between being on the in or on the out of the faction imo and it's something that could be fodder for a good story. It also highlights the fact that the traditions are a highly imperfect system of organization and one which arguably causes more problems then benefits for the Council Magi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T16:04:18-07:00","id":1399686,"title":"","content":"And yet, the imputus for the name change from Euthanatos to Chakravanti... <br /> <br /> &quot;alright people, we're going to be super progressive: One culturally specific name to another culture's specific name.&quot; <br /> <br /> I can't imagine many mages going along with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T16:12:44-07:00","id":1399687,"title":"","content":"The thing is, the reason for the name change is ultimately that Euthanatos never made much since compared to Chakravanti.<br /> <br /> The traditions philosophy is the most ascendent on the Indian sub-continent, the majority of the tradition are likely if Indian origin, and the 'Euthanatoi' as a name does a good job of representing the stereotype of the karmic serial killer but that stereotype overshadowed the tradition, a problem that's been there for multiple editions.<br /> <br /> The Chakravanti has always made more sense as a name, has always represented the majority of the tradition's culture and membership, and is a metatextual step away from the stereotype of the Euthanatos Death-Cultist with their silenced pistol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T16:31:37-07:00","id":1399690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1399686#post1399686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, the imputus for the name change from Euthanatos to Chakravanti...<br /> <br /> &quot;alright people, we're going to be super progressive: One culturally specific name to another culture's specific name.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can't imagine many mages going along with that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They're not taking &quot;another culture's name&quot; though. They're taking THEIR name. Both Tradition books make it fairly clear that the majority of the Tradition is made up of South Asian people, based on South Asian philosophy. Chakravanti was established as the original name in the first Tradition book.<br /> <br /> They may have chosen the &quot;Euthanatos&quot; name in order to fit better in the Traditions themselves, especially with the Hermetics who claim Greek and Egyptian origins for their practice, but the Greek death cultists have always been the minority. There's very little focus on the elements of Greek and Celtic religion that the European members follow, compared to the bulk of the material is about the Wheel, Jhor, the war with the Akashics, and other elements that are very specific to the Indian setting.<br /> <br /> There's no indication that any of the individual members are particularly enamored with the &quot;Euthanatos&quot; name, and most do seem inclined to want to separate themselves from the misdeeds of Voormas, Helekar, and other elements of the old stereotype, so they've got a perfectly reasonable justification to reclaim their old, ACCURATE name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T16:39:51-07:00","id":1399692,"title":"","content":"Not sure what these \u201cCeltic beliefs\u201d are supposed to be. There are some hints from Greek and Roman authors that early Celtic-speaking peoples believed in a form of reincarnation. That\u2019s literally all we have to go on and probably the only reason the Euthanatos writeup mentions it at all, to make it seem more international when it\u2019s clearly based on their impressions of some Indian stuff. <br /> <br /> What\u2019s really going on is an attempt to address the setting\u2019s Eurocentrism, where traditions had European names and concepts out of proportion with the global population. That\u2019s come in for a good bit of justifiable criticism over the years. And, frankly, do we really think arguing against that is a good look? No matter what your intentions, complaining that the setting is getting less Eurocentric and is incorporating more non-European names doesn\u2019t put one in very good company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T16:48:08-07:00","id":1399695,"title":"","content":"There's one viewpoint character in the first Tradition books that's a Celtic follower of Morrigan, if I recall correctly. But certainly they don't seem to be a very large percentage of the group. It's rather like how you could easily put a Germanic Norse shaman in the Dreamspeakers/Kha'vadi, given their practice, but that character will never be the majority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T22:12:02-07:00","id":1399733,"title":"","content":"The factions within the Euthanatoi, as of the Revised Edition, are the Chakravanti, the Madzimbabwe (focus on sub-Saharan ancestor veneration), the Hierochthonoi (Greek mages who deal with the more \u201cearthy\u201d chthonic gods of their mythology, and particularly with the Fates), the Aided (celtic bards who are masters of the Geasa), and the Vrati (defined less by culture and more by proficiency, these are the \u201cSpecial Forces\u201d of the Tradition). Those are the main factions, with the Indian mages easily being the majority and referenced as the ones who \u201cdefine the Tradition's identity\u201d. Then you've got a smattering of others such as Yggdrasil's Keepers (Nordic mages who use runes to reveal and preserve Wyrd), the Pallotino (Italian death-mages), Yum Cimil (Mayan mages), and so on. <br /> <br /> Note that the Aided fit into the Tradition not so much because they're about <i>death</i>, but rather because they're about <i>fate</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-29-2020, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T22:35:12-07:00","id":1399736,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Dataweaver! I knew I was forgetting important details, but I didn't have my book in front of me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T00:42:58-07:00","id":1399749,"title":"","content":"Indians in reality are far too devided, linguistically or culturally. Maybe they voted with FPTP...<br /> <br /> Imagine you called all Abrahamic religions after their largest group, Catholics (Maybe Shia, but I don't really know how sects work and if they should impact that) even though you could call them abrahamic faiths or something like that and upset nobody. <br /> <br /> Dreamspeakers, as lowkey racist as that is, at least has a pretty broad umbrella and doesn't say anyone group under it is inferior to another group under it.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's very much a move of &quot;The Traditions are eurocentric, Let's give them diversity names!&quot;<br /> It's clearly something of author fiat, rather than something that would happen (unless they did FPTP, but do mages really hate themselves that much?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T08:52:48-07:00","id":1399843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1399749#post1399749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's very much a move of &amp;quot;The Traditions are eurocentric, Let's give them diversity names!&amp;quot;<br /> It's clearly something of author fiat, rather than something that would happen (unless they did FPTP, but do mages really hate themselves that much?)</div> </div> </div> </div>While I get your sentiment, since the names are there, I'd like to think of them as a result of magical thinking, with the new tradition leaders coming together saying something like &quot;We can't seem to get our act together. Euthanatos keeps getting into dark and deadly crap, Dreamspeakers have almost walked out on the conventions... Let's fix this. Let's start from the ground up. Let's change what we call each other too. It will help ease relations, help us be what we want to be, and when the technocracy did their convention name changes, they got shit done. &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T09:11:34-07:00","id":1399847,"title":"","content":"And it's not like this would be the first time Traditions have changed their names. The Euthanatoi were originally called the Chakravanti; the Cult of Ecstasy was originally called the Seers of Chronos. And like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12480_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12480\" data-vbnamecard=\"12480\">Spacecat</a> says, the New Millennium timeline assumes that the Traditions have reacted to the loss of their elders by attempting a reboot of sorts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T09:15:23-07:00","id":1399849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1399749#post1399749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indians in reality are far too devided, linguistically or culturally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not too divided to agree on Sanskrit as their classical language.<br /> <br /> But really, this is just another red herring. The Tradition isn\u2019t the republic of India. It\u2019s a group whose number measure in the hundreds, not the millions. Nor are its members going to be practitioners of normal Indian religions. The Tradition basically <i>is </i>a cult in itself.<br /> <br /> Also, Indian/Sanskrit terms and ideas have been hugely popular in occult circles for well over a century. I\u2019d go so far a to say they\u2019re more attractive to many people than Greek ones. You keep positing impediments that don\u2019t actually exist.<br /> <br /> Also, sometimes people just shift their terminology over time. It didn\u2019t take long for most people to start saying Mumbai instead of Bombay, or Myanmar instead of Burma, or Beijing instead of Peking. That didn\u2019t require an act of Congress. No vote was needed. Once they start to perceive that a different name is catching on, most people will go with it, if only not to be left behind.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also the fact that people who are too rigid in their thinking aren\u2019t likely to Awaken in the first place. That requires a certain modicum of conceptual plasticity. And this actually becomes <i>more </i>true the more advanced they become, not less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 06-29-2020, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T09:16:17-07:00","id":1399850,"title":"","content":"Also, with regards to the Euthanatos comment above, Hebrew &quot;avrahami&quot; seems an appropriate term, which would be &quot;abrahamic&quot; in English and &quot;aliibrahimia&quot; in Arabic, and probably similar in other languages. It's possible the various euthanatos groups see no real problem with the &quot;people of the wheel term&quot; chakravanti much the same way &quot;euthanatos&quot; didn't used to bother them. Heck, maybe it's even mostly just a brand name change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T03:57:02-07:00","id":1401086,"title":"","content":"To go back to the discussion of the first page how M5 should develop.<br /> I would say like VTMV it should start as an Orphan chronic which would make even now more sense then in VTM.<br /> Then as next I would say bring a Technocracy Book about the low lvl Technocrats as an Alternative and as Frenemies for the Mages. This should show, how the normal people of the Technocracy think and make them see, that this war is a matter of perspective. Eg from my chronic:<br /> The new girlfriend of the best bro of an character is an NWO that want to subdue his friend because she is afraid he is only an evil mind manipulator that conspire with vampires and want to keep her boyfriend safe from him. The mage sees in her an evil government surpressor that want to indoctrinate his bro and keep him from seeing the wonders of the world and want him only to believe in a bland wonderless world.<br /> <br /> Next I would bring either Alliance or Traditions, depending on if the former are now part of the latter to slowly open the mind to how much bigger the world is and giving a mythical alternative with more order. Then as next book I would bring a book about the Ascension War and show now not on Low Lvl but on big scale how the situation right now is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T08:17:28-07:00","id":1401121,"title":"","content":"I have to admit, I'd be disappointed if M5 went with the all Orphan approach. The Traditions are not the Camarilla, and in my opinion, focusing on orphans only severely curtails the type of Mage that you can play. It'd be like if V5 expected you to start by playing only Caitiff.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't necessarily expect them to go all in on the Ascension War, but it wouldn't feel like an edition of Mage to me without the Order of Hermes, Akashics, et al.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T09:01:09-07:00","id":1401132,"title":"","content":"I'd agree with you if M5 went with Orphans as described in M1, M2, or MRev; but if they go with M20-style Orphans, that's a whole different matter. See the sample characters in <b>Book of Secrets</b> (pp.176\u2013187): other than Sanjay Sachdeva, none of these characters state an allegiance to any faction in the game; and in the case of Tanisha Royale, it's explicitly stated that she <i>isn't</i> an Akashic disciple. All but one of these characters could easily be Orphans in the M20 sense. <br /> <br /> And it's in <i>that</i> sense that I could see M5 focusing on \u201cOrphans\u201d. Not the practitioners of gutter magick of the first three editions that are now primarily a Hollow Ones thing; but mages that differ from the Traditionists, Disparates, and Technocrats primarily in that they're not associated with any secret societies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T09:29:24-07:00","id":1401134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1401132#post1401132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it's in <i>that</i> sense that I could see M5 focusing on \u201cOrphans\u201d. Not the practitioners of gutter magick of the first three editions that are now primarily a Hollow Ones thing; but mages that differ from the Traditionists, Disparates, and Technocrats primarily in that they're not associated with any secret societies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree. This is what I ment and more or less described for an Orphan Chronic in M20. Concretly said an Orphan focused M5 means there is only rudimentary description about Traditions, Technocray, Disparate Alliance and the Rest of the WoD but mainly focusing on what it means about being a Mage, how you use magick, what to do to make your city the center of a Mage chronic and what is need to do, to create your own magical believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T09:48:02-07:00","id":1401139,"title":"","content":"But the secret societies are part of what makes a mage a mage. Orphans are an option, sure, and there's nothing wrong with taking that option in a game. But I like playing Hermetics and Akashics and Euthanatoics.<br /> <br /> I LIKE the secret societies, whether or not we incorporate the larger ascension war.<br /> <br /> Starting as an orphan and gradually getting introduced to the larger universe sounds like a great chronicle, but that's really just one type of chronicle.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean I wouldn't love to see supplements like you're describing, but IMO, the core rulebook should give me at least enough information about where the Traditions are at this point in time to allow me to play one at the start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 07-05-2020, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T10:22:42-07:00","id":1401143,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I'm not suggesting that the secret societies be left out of the core book entirely; but I could see reducing them to an appendix that gives only the essence of what each one is, with even the one-page write-ups of each Tradition, Convention, and Craft being postponed for an appropriate supplement. Instead, include something like the Arcane Approaches write-ups found in <b>Mage Made Easy</b>, and relegate individual Traditions to something like \u201c<i>Society of Ether:</i> Gadgeteers and Mad Scientists who deal in rejected and fringe sciences and seek to expand mankind's horizons until everything is possible.\u201d (<i>Gadgeteer</i> and <i>Mad Scientist</i> are two Approaches found in <b>Mage Made Easy</b>, and would provide the heavy lifting in terms of how to make and roleplay such a character.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T14:38:02-07:00","id":1401193,"title":"","content":"I'd rather see changes in the Council than a focus on Orphans... And I don't mean name changes. I mean drastic changes with lasting consequences, like a true attempt at a proper unified system of awakened magick with players as the first results of these; or actual mixed tradition groups with solid ascension war projects and goals, like disembodiment cure avatar storm weapinization and protection from it or vaccination, local paradigm shifting, magical transhumanist projects, or their very own magic future pogrom; fun crazy stuff like that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T17:20:53-07:00","id":1401228,"title":"","content":"With all of the Rogue Council/Sphinx/New Horizon Council stuff, it seems counter-intuitive to reduce the Traditions to an appendix. This is the point where player characters would really have the opportunity to take part in how it all develops. M20 did the right thing by being primarily metaplot agnostic, IMO, but I'm hoping M5 does like V5 and moves everything forward.<br /> <br /> But Mage isn't like Vampire. Vampire can focus on the Anarchs, because clan is different from sect. You can be a Ventrue or a Toreador but not be in the Camarilla. Mage doesn't really work that way. The Traditions aren't just political bodies, they're also the foundation of a Mage's entire practice. Not everyone is interested in playing a self-taught Orphan with a jury-rigged practice. <br /> <br /> That doesn't mean we can't play Mark Hallward Gillan style rogues of course, but we still need to know what we're rebelling against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T21:56:00-07:00","id":1401270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1401228#post1401228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Mage doesn't really work that way. The Traditions aren't just political bodies, they're also the foundation of a Mage's entire practice. Not everyone is interested in playing a self-taught Orphan with a jury-rigged practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who came into mage in Revised edition, I always found that a little... paradoxical. So if I am an unawakened-but-soon-to-be-awakened pagan, who worships the Goddess in his own way but doesn't incorporate blood sacrifice (because who does?) how do I get from there... to the Verbena? Does an awakened Verbena have to take me under her wing and teach me a lot of stuff and be like &quot;Hey, if you really want to awaken, you gotta use blood. Like a lot. It's really cool.&quot; And then DING! I see the truth and now I get to awaken? Of course not.<br /> <br /> But if everyone awakens in their own way and the Traditions way of doing things isn't special, then what's with all the blood sacrifice in the Vebena? How do we get from the vast majority of modern neopagan practice NOT involving blood sacrifice, to the largest secret society of neopagans being all about the blood?<br /> <br /> And this isn't knocking blood magic by any means. You do you. I am just saying, it's kind of a specific quirk of that tradition that doesn't really make sense.<br /> <br /> So to me, the traditions only really make sense as a political body if they are a group of umbrellas, where many people of similar concerns can gather. I don't feel that they can be the foundation of people's magick, because their teachings aren't special and don't cause people to awaken, and they are all secret. Everyone has to awaken on their own in their own way. Or at least, that's the only way that makes sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T23:12:43-07:00","id":1401281,"title":"","content":"I don't think we're in disagreement per se. I think every single one of the Traditions operates as an umbrella in some capacity. The individual tradition books talk about different factions under each umbrella that use different approaches. <br /> <br /> But if we're working with the standard mage setting, then our characters use magic according to their beliefs. The advantage to the Traditions in that respect is that we have centuries of practices that are reinforced by the individual group in question. Obviously an individual would provide his own spin on his practice, but there's a lot of psychological reinforcement involved with using old grimoires or artifacts.<br /> <br /> Also, the Verbena aren't NEO-pagans. They're meant to be the real deal. The original witch archetype. The Old Faith folks who bring the practices of their ancestors in the present day. And at least as the Mage setting establishes it, those old rites were a lot more bloody and earthy than modern Neo-Pagan rituals. Et cetera. Neo-Pagans are included under the Verbena umbrella, but a lot of the older practitioners (some of whom may well have been alive when these original practices were new) look at them a bit askance.<br /> <br /> Obviously you can play a neo-pagan orphan or Hollow One, and truth be told, that probably would be a more comfortable fit for many neo-pagans than the Verbena are. But I don't really see the appeal to that. If I'm going to play an old school witch, I'd rather go all out and embrace the Tradition, warts and all. Similarly, I don't see why I would bother making an orphan martial artist (though they're definitely possible too), when I have the entire history and complexity of the Akashayana to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T01:22:09-07:00","id":1401293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1401228#post1401228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Mage isn't like Vampire. Vampire can focus on the Anarchs, because clan is different from sect. You can be a Ventrue or a Toreador but not be in the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is an analogy that I can't really comment on, as my familiarity with Vampire is almost null. I mention this only in case you have the mistaken idea that I'm trying to make Mage more like Vampire. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1401228#post1401228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage doesn't really work that way. The Traditions aren't just political bodies, they're also the foundation of a Mage's entire practice. Not everyone is interested in playing a self-taught Orphan with a jury-rigged practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the whole point of M20's new Focus system is that the Traditions <i>aren't</i> the foundation of a mage's entire practice. That is, unlike earlier editions where \u201cmad scientist\u201d and \u201cSon of Ether\u201d were pretty much considered synonyms, where if you wanted to play the former you had to look up the Theory and Practice sections in the write-up of the latter, M20's revision to the whole Focus and Paradigm thing made it possible to design someone with the Practice of Weird Science without ever once going anywhere near the Sons of Ether write-up. <br /> <br /> And the whole point of my post is that M20's Orphans <i>aren't</i> about \u201cjury-rigged practice\u201d anymore. That's handled by the Practice of Gutter Magic now; and while it's more common among the Orphans than it is among other groups, it's no longer presented as the default for them. <br /> <br /> In fact, in an M5 as I envision it, the term \u201cOrphan\u201d wouldn't appear in the core book. The first time you'd see it would be in the supplement that fleshes out the Traditions, and it would be made clear that it's a derogatory term used by the Traditions to stereotype the independent mages described in the core book as a bunch of know-nothings playing around with powers they couldn't possibly understand because they don't have the benefit of the Traditions' patronage. <br /> <br /> Put another way, \u201cindependent mages are Orphans, who use jury-rigged practices\u201d would be presented as Traditionist arrogance, not fact. The fact would be that most independent mages would <i>not</i> be what Traditionists call \u201cOrphans\u201d, and that the Traditions aren't nearly as important as they think they are; and in terms of the practice of magic, the Traditions don't bring nearly as much to the table as they think they do. <br /> <br /> And lest you misunderstand, there <i>is</i> one thing of great value that the Traditions absolutely <i>do</i> bring to the table: they're the \u201cecumenicals\u201d of the setting, the mages who have raised the commingling of different practices to an art form through the pioneering of the Esperanto of the Practices. The Verbena aren't better at being witches than the independent witches are, nor are the Choristers better at being devotees than independent devotees are; but Choristers and Verbena are better at working together than independent devotees and witches are. And that would be touched on in the core book in the section that sketches out the Traditions as a group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T07:07:49-07:00","id":1401337,"title":"","content":"I'm not in love with the idea of M5 being about playing Orphans...however, to make justice of the Traditions AND the Technocracy you need more than a few pages. Traditions figthing against the technos it's less intuitive now than it was in the 90' (esp. if you don't want them being souless, and/or the Core being &quot;Traditional propaganda&quot;) ... and I wouldn't want to reduce Mage philosophical conundrums as a figth against satanists (if you get what I mean). All of this really could use some explaining. And that would detract from the pages explaining the sistem and what you can do with it, which it's what I really would want from a Core. In that sense, it migth be better to have the book being very general about things, and leaving the nuances of the Factions for future suplements.<br /> <br /> Orphans are good for this because they see the Ascencion War from the outside. They can interact with these as antagonists and other significant NPCs until it's time to reveal all the big stuff in the next book (bonus points if there are actually big stuff to reveal. That is: stuff going on in the Factions, advances in the War, plans to trully rock the WoD).<br /> <br /> Not long ago this would have been impossible because you needed the Traditions as a guide to understand what kind of mages you can make, but as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> says, this is made feasible thanks to M20 decoupling Tradition and Focus. That being said, I don't think that the Core should waste pages emphasizing the &quot;importance&quot; of Independants. Obviously they won't call themselves Orphans. That IS a derogatory (this ain't new, several old books already talk about this), and shouldn't appear in a book that's not written from the perspective of a larger faction. But that doesn't need to (and in my opinion shouldn't) mean that the factions, or the War, are somehow less important for the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-06-2020, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T08:37:24-07:00","id":1401350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1401337#post1401337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not in love with the idea of M5 being about playing Orphans...however, to make justice of the Traditions AND the Technocracy you need more than a few pages. Traditions figthing against the technos it's less intuitive now than it was in the 90' (esp. if you don't want them being souless, and/or the Core being &quot;Traditional propaganda&quot;) ... and I wouldn't want to reduce Mage philosophical conundrums as a figth against satanists (if you get what I mean). All of this really could use some explaining. And that would detract from the pages explaining the system and what you can do with it, which it's what I really would want from a Core. In that sense, it migth be better to have the book being very general about things, and leaving the nuances of the Factions for future suplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I've been trying to say. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1401337#post1401337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orphans are good for this because they see the Ascencion War from the outside. They can interact with these as antagonists and other significant NPCs until it's time to reveal all the big stuff in the next book (bonus points if there are actually big stuff to reveal. That is: stuff going on in the Factions, advances in the War, plans to trully rock the WoD).</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, this. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1401337#post1401337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not long ago this would have been impossible because you needed the Traditions as a guide to understand what kind of mages you can make, but as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> says, this is made feasible thanks to M20 decoupling Tradition and Focus. That being said, I don't think that the Core should waste pages emphasizing the &quot;importance&quot; of Independants. Obviously they won't call themselves Orphans. That IS a derogatory (this ain't new, several old books already talk about this), and shouldn't appear in a book that's not written from the perspective of a larger faction. But that doesn't need to (and in my opinion shouldn't) mean that the factions, or the War, are somehow less important for the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this, mostly. In particular, my argument hasn't been that the core book should sing the praises of the mages formerly known as Orphans and denigrate the ones who have joined the Ascension War. But M20 is over 600 pages long, and that's <i>way</i> too Long for a core book; M5 is going to need to be shorter, which means a combination of off-loading a lot of material into supplements and ruthlessly streamlining what stays. And a <i>major</i> page-saver would be to put off most of the Ascension War and related factions material for supplements. <br /> <br /> And that leaves the default protagonists of the core book being the independent mages, with the Traditions, Technocracy, and Disparates appearing in a minimal-sketch form that's enough for gamers coming from earlier editions to be able to play them (which, again, is possible because the Arcane Approaches do the heavy lifting for everyone equally, whether they're Traditionists, Technocrats, Disparates, or none of the above) while gamers who are jumping on with M5 will get a chance to \u201cget their feet wet\u201d with mages who <i>aren't</i> immersed in the Ascension War before moving on to that later on \u2014 or not, if they decide that they're fine with things without it. <br /> <br /> And frankly, I don't consider \u201cindependent mages usually aren't Orphans\u201d to be \u201cemphasizing the \u2018importance\u2019 of independents\u201d, especially since I don't think the point would need to be explicitly addressed. It would be handled <i>implicitly</i>, by the fact that the term Orphan wouldn't even appear in the core book (and note that I haven't suggested an alternate name; there oughtn't be a need for one) and by the fact that the earlier editions' factions would be presented as an optional element of the game rather than as a central feature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T10:33:26-07:00","id":1401367,"title":"","content":"Something else I'd like to see in M5: move the Focus section into character creation, with the decision of what your Paradigm, Practice, and Instruments are being placed in Step One, and with the Paradigm, Practice, and Instrument write-ups being placed right alongside the write-ups for Essence (and, if it makes it into the core book, Resonance). In the interest of ruthless streamlining, I'd even consider the idea of scrapping Nature and Demeanor, and having Paradigm take over that system nich\u00e9.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T23:04:58-07:00","id":1401434,"title":"","content":"I agree with you on Paradigm and Practice. I think they're a good fit for the introductory parts of character creation, which always struck me as dealing more with general concepts/role playing details. I think I'd hold off on Instruments though, until after Spheres/Arete. Instruments are...is? a more detail-oriented part of the process, and I think that the player's choice of instruments are often affected by the abilities, backgrounds and spheres that they've chosen. (especially personal or unique instruments).<br /> <br /> Intellectually speaking, I think the idea of scrapping Nature and Demeanor makes some sense, but the gamer in me is very resistant to losing a potential source of replenished willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T01:15:42-07:00","id":1401445,"title":"","content":"The way I'm envisioning it, you <i>wouldn't</i> lose a potential source of replenished Willpower; rather, that would be what Paradigm (and Essence?) does: if you do something that affirms your Paradigm (and/or is in accordance with your Essence?), you regain Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T05:17:26-07:00","id":1401463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1401367#post1401367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something else I'd like to see in M5: move the Focus section into character creation, with the decision of what your Paradigm, Practice, and Instruments are being placed in Step One, and with the Paradigm, Practice, and Instrument write-ups being placed right alongside the write-ups for Essence (and, if it makes it into the core book, Resonance). In the interest of ruthless streamlining, I'd even consider the idea of scrapping Nature and Demeanor, and having Paradigm take over that system nich\u00e9.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt they'd let go of Nature/Demeanor entirely, but yes, I think putting those elements up front is a definite good idea.<br /> <br /> That said, I think we will have a better idea of what M5 will look like AFTER W5. There likelyw ill be some trendlines to follow as we see more of what the vision for each game is. Part of the issue is that our current datapoints are a bit scattered and not really data points - we have V5, which has gone through a couple different creative hands since its release, and we have M20 which may or may not be indicative of ANYTHING that is to come after. But, when we get W5, we'll have two 5th ed &quot;lines&quot; out and can see what kind of focus the new management has for their games; not a guarantee everything will carry over into M5, but it will be helpful to have two adaptations and see which way things go. <br /> <br /> Also... there's the real consideration of IRL factors. WtA is arguably the most overtly political of all the games, bar none - it has a very, VERY clear set of core messages about environmentalism, race, and other factors built into the setting and plot. However, Mage has had political undercurrents as well, but without necessarily always intending it. The naming issue brought up certainly is one, but the more relevant in the modern age (and arguably right now) may be the issues with the Technocrats as objective villains. Not only is this something that's been revisited time and again by the line, but it's something that, given a lot of issues of late, could be something that the game runners wish to avoid - while I doubt the portrayal of the Technocracy is largely or even a little to blame for certain antiscience attitudes in modern culture, it is an issue that may need to be re-examined as we move into a future hypothetical M5. <br /> <br /> One thing that DOES seem likely is that, regardless of who the focus is on, the main factions (i.e. Traditions) will be around but not in a good place. V5 had most of the clans still around, though we've yet to get two of the thirteen core clans fully statted and may not get the Ravnos as more than a mention in a Loresheet (which is... understandable given their history on an out-of-game level). W5 hasn't come out yet, but indications are that Earthblood is set in a W5-like world, which still recognizes breed, auspice, and tribe to some extent given the symbols we've seen representing the main character (and, a lof the direction hinted at thus far by the announcement of the publishing licensee for W5 and the stuff we've seen for Earthblood all hint that the BNS LARP setting is somewhat of a middle step towards the vision of W5 - not all the elements may make it over, but if you compare that early material to BNS WtA you do see some definite lining-up, which makes sense since it was finished under Paradox; compare to the BNS version of VtM, which has some similarities - some part of the Assamites/Banu Haqim siding with the Tower, a large Lasombra contingent leaving the Sabbat - but also a TON of differences - the Giovanni and Setites create a new sect rather than the Setites going Ministry, the various descendants of the Cappadocians aren't coming together as they did in V5, the Sabbat are still around but in a cold war with the other factions, and so on. These differences are likely because of a different vision by the prior IP owners when BNS licensed VtM - where they were fine doling out aspects of the game for different lines and worlds, letting OP do V20 and BNS do a LARP ruleset. Given that W5 is going in a direction that seems to line up with, or at least is parallel to, the setting established in the LARP rules, and given the trailers we've seen, the old divisions/subsplats for Werewolves likely still exist as clans still exist for vampires, so I doubt the traditions will go anywhere, but they definitely will be suffering in the wake of the Second Inquisition (possibly less than Vampires, though).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T17:03:05-07:00","id":1401574,"title":"","content":"I think an issue, though I might be strawmanning here, is will the magick system still be recognizable? V5 presents Disciplines and Sorcery in a manner completely different from the established (and in my opinion, genius) system that came before it. Replacing it with something that might suit someone's tastes better from a mechanical/game design standpoint, but from a lore/metaphyics standpoint they have really gone against the grain. <br /> <br /> What if spheres just become a grouping for related but very specific powers? IE the life sphere's first level comes with a wound healing power, a sickness healing power and a cosmetic power. Potence used to just give you all-around movie-style super-strength , but now it offers hyper-specific strength themed powers per level (Jump high, do more damage to people, do this climbing trick) They function a lot like werewolf gifts now. <br /> Spheres are even more broad than disciplines were. Looking at V5, why wouldn't spheres instead become ten-thousand very specific powers rather than 'I can do anything my spheres say I can do' ? Would you guys welcome this change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T17:46:08-07:00","id":1401582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1401574#post1401574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think an issue, though I might be strawmanning here, is will the magick system still be recognizable? V5 presents Disciplines and Sorcery in a manner completely different from the established (and in my opinion, genius) system that came before it. Replacing it with something that might suit someone's tastes better from a mechanical/game design standpoint, but from a lore/metaphyics standpoint they have really gone against the grain.<br /> <br /> What if spheres just become a grouping for related but very specific powers? IE the life sphere's first level comes with a wound healing power, a sickness healing power and a cosmetic power. Potence used to just give you all-around movie-style super-strength , but now it offers hyper-specific strength themed powers per level (Jump high, do more damage to people, do this climbing trick) They function a lot like werewolf gifts now.<br /> Spheres are even more broad than disciplines were. Looking at V5, why wouldn't spheres instead become ten-thousand very specific powers rather than 'I can do anything my spheres say I can do' ? Would you guys welcome this change?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly not. Mage Ascension whas from my impression always this &quot;Magic is freedom and creativity (and the sleepers believe) is the limit.&quot; If there would be strictly specificied powers we would have stayed at VtM where the Disciples fullfilled the role and Blood Magic worked without Paradoxon, because it is the dream of the Technocracy, a system which is totally standartified, specified and researched into the tiniest little bit so the world accepted it despite what the dreamers believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 07-09-2020, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T23:46:16-07:00","id":1401630,"title":"","content":"M5's Magick system needs to be as flexible as possible; one of the primary draws of the game is how versatile the magick system is. Some things I'd change about the current system: <br /> <br /> First, swap the placement of Spheres and Focus in the \u201cCasting Magick, Step by Step\u201d section: <i>Focus: How your character does it</i> should be presented in <i>Step One: Effect</i>, as part of how you describe the Effect; and <i>Spheres: The Foundation of Each Effect</i> should be in <i>Step Two: Ability</i> as part of determining if you have what it takes to attempt the Effect. I'd also move the <i>Wild Talent</i> section from the end of the Sphere write-ups to the end of the <i>Spheres: the Foundation of Each Effect</i> part of <i>Step Two: Ability</i>, as Wild Talent isn't so much about defining Sphere-like traits as it is about knowing when it's appropriate to ignore the Sphere requirements for crafting an Effect and what to do instead. <br /> <br /> Second, <i>Step One: Effect</i> should have a subsection about the magnitude of the Effect. This section would be where you discuss how many successes the Effect should require: that is, setting the Magnitude would answer the question of whether this is a Simple, Standard, Difficult, Impressive, Mighty, Outlandish, or Godlike Feat. This would also be where you point out the implications of a given Magnitude of Effect: Magnitudes below Mighty might be doable in a single roll; but if you don't want to risk it, you can cast them as Rituals, which count as rites that will take minutes to perform. Mighty, Outlandish, and Godlike Feats will almost certainly have to be cast as Rituals, with Mighty Feats counting as ceremonies that take hours to perform and Outlandish or Godlike Feats counting as Great Works that are measured in days. You don't have to go into the specific rules at this point; just indicate that if you don't think your mage can achieve the Effect in a single roll, expect that crafting the Effect will take a while. <br /> <br /> The idea here is to bring Magickal Feats more into the forefront, rather than being something that's buried in the middle of Step Three: defining an Effect should involve deciding how \u201cbig\u201d that Effect will be. In this same vein, I'd have M5's Effect write-ups include hope big of a Feat each Effect is: even if 99% of them say \u201cStandard Feat\u201d, it gets the reader in the habit of thinking not just in terms of how many Sphere levels are required, but also how many successes are needed. <br /> <br /> <i>Rotes, Procedures, and Other Prepared Effects</i> and <i>Knowing and Learning Rotes</i> would go to <i>Step Two: Ability</i>, while <i>Coincidental Magick vs. Vulgar Magick</i> would move to <i>Step One: Effect</i>. Both sections would undergo some changes: I'd at least consider the possibility of replacing the Coincidental vs. Vulgar split with the Subtle/Uncanny/Extreme split that Brucato describes in <b>Mage Made Easy</b>. There <i>would</i> be other changes to the Paradox mechanics; but in Step One, the focus would solely be on deciding how subtle or blatant the Effect is. <br /> <br /> In the <i>Step Two: Ability</i> subsection on Rotes, I would make the controversial decision to add system benefits for knowing a Rote, and an experience point cost for learning one. The fine points would be addressed later; but at this point in the process, the key feature would be that knowing our having access to a Rote can substitute for insufficient levels of Spheres and even Arete. That is, if you don't have enough dots in your Spheres to craft the Effect, but you <i>do</i> have access to the Effect as a Rote, you can still perform it. And if you have access to the Rote, your dice pool is the higher of your Arete or the highest Sphere in the Rote. <br /> <br /> The primary motivation for <i>this</i> change is to provide an alternative to Sorcery, so that you don't need to write a massive new edition of <b>Sorcerer</b> in order to include acolytes and extraordinary citizens who know a trick or two (or three or four) but aren't Awakened. And the idea would be that the more you raise your Arete and Spheres, the less important Rotes become, possibly even to the point that you get a \u201crefund\u201d on the experience points you spent on them in the form of a discount to the cost of raising your Spheres to the level that the Rote is no longer needed. <br /> <br /> I would split up the <i>Mundane Skills and Magickal Effects</i> section, with <i>Abilities Enhancing Magick</i> staying in <i>Step Two: Ability</i> while <i>Magick Enhancing Abilities</i> would be moved into the section in Common Magickal Effects \u2014 i.e., what can you do with Magick? I would also add an entry for \u201csuitable Ability: -1 to -3\u201d on the Magickal Difficulty Modifiers table, under Tools and Rituals, while streamlining its entry in Step Two to just \u201cif you have dots in a suitable mundane ability, it can help you with the crafting of the Effect\u201d, with the system for doing so being incorporated into\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Step Three: Roll</b><br /> First, I'd scrap the notion that how subtle or blatant the Effect is has any bearing on how difficult the casting is; the differences between them would be handled solely by how much Paradox they generate. Set the Difficulty as \u201chighest Sphere in the Effect + 4\u201d. Second, I'd scrap the \u201cmodifiers can't adjust the modifier by more than \u00b13\u201d \u2014 but I'd <i>keep</i> the Minimum Difficulty of 3, and reinforce it as a universal limit, not just \u201cif the Effect is cast on Earth\u201d. <br /> <br /> Step Three is where the reference charts come in, and I'd want this section to have a paragraph for each one (with a handful of exceptions, like handling all of the Instrument-related modifiers together). The point is that there shouldn't be an entry on any of the Magickal Reference Charts that doesn't get addressed in <i>Step Three: Roll</i>. <br /> <br /> I'd also rename the Magickal Feats chart as Magnitude, and revise it with two additional columns: a Difficulty Modifier column (which would replace the \u201coutlandish to god-like feat\u201d entry on the Magickal Difficulty Modifiers table) and a Ritual column (which would be one of rite, ceremony, or great work). The idea would be to put all of the system effects of choosing a particular Magnitude in one place. <br /> <br /> A few entries on the Magickal Difficulty Modifiers chart would be revised: <br /> <br /> \u2022 \u201cUsing personal item from target\u201d would be moved to the Correspondence Sphere Ranges table, and would represent how the difficulty of the Effect is influenced by the level of Connection you establish with the subject, assuming that you incorporate even a single dot of Correspondence into the Effect (though a single dot wouldn't be enough to let you extend the range of your Effect; you'd get the Difficulty Modifier, but only if the subject is near enough to affect without Correspondence). <br /> <br /> \u2022 \u201cSpending Extra Time\u201d: this ought to be -1 per additional turn on an instant crafting, per additional five minutes on a rite, per additional hour on a ceremony, and per additional five hours on a great work. <br /> <br /> \u2022 \u201cDomino Effect\u201d: I'd scrap this, and replace it with a system where excessive use of subtle effects eventually start being counted as if they were uncanny and start generating Paradox. <br /> <br /> The Degrees of Success table should revise Partial Success from \u201croughly half of the Suggested Successes\u201d to \u201cat least one success, but less than the Suggested Successes\u201d. You might also need separate tables for instant effects and for Rituals, as \u201cmage can keep going\u201d doesn't really make sense for an instant Effect. <br /> <br /> I'd rename the Base Damage or Duration table as the Base Potency table; and I'd add columns for Area and Targets. As with the current table, you only get one column as the Base for a given Effect. I'd also rename the Optional Dividing Successes Rule table as the Additional Aspects table, and add an entry for Area. I'd also scrap the \u201cpermanent\u201d Duration, both in terms of Base Potency and Additional Aspects: if you want an Effect to be permanent, you need to use something like the \u201ccrafting a Wonder\u201d rule. <br /> <br /> I have some thoughts about the \u201cI Disbelieve!\u201d table and Countermagick; but I'll address that in a separate thread. <br /> <br /> <b>Paradox:</b><br /> Replace the separate dice pool with Paradox dice, similar to the Hunger Dice in V5: if a Paradox die comes up as a 1 or 10, you get a Backlash, with each such die counting as one \u201cBacklash Success\u201d. (If you have more Paradox Dice than the dice pool you're supposed to roll, replace the extra Paradox Dice with \u201cPure Paradox Dice\u201d: roll them along with the Paradox Dice, but ignore them when determining the roll's success or failure; only pay attention to them for the purpose of determining Backlash.) <br /> <br /> The idea here is to streamline, and hopefully speed up, the casting-and-Backlash system by combining the two dice pools: assemble one pool, roll it, then read it twice, once for the Effect's successes and again for the Backlash. <br /> <br /> For the effects of a Backlash, scrap the existing system entirely. Instead, the Storyteller comes up with an Effect conforming to the character's Focus and related to the Effect that the character was just trying to craft. An Onset of Quiet is a mind-altering Effect; Paradox Flaws are effectively Life, Matter, or Forces Effects; Paradox Spirits and Realms are Spirit Effects, based on summoning and stepping sideways respectively; Physical Backlash could be just about anything. The Storyteller shouldn't feel too constrained by the mage's Spheres; a Backlash is, in effect, a malicious Wild Talent, so he's justified in going a few dots beyond the mage if he thinks it to be appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-23-2020, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T15:28:21-07:00","id":1401785,"title":"","content":"Just for the sake of speculation, I wanted to know your opinions about dividing the factions, and the ascension war, alongside the three basic ways of understanding magick and the universe: sience, faith and mysticism. I don't remember where I saw this triad, but I always though it would be cool seeing history as a result of the clash between these viewpoints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T15:39:56-07:00","id":1401790,"title":"","content":"Science, faith, and Magic was the tagline for Sorcerers Crusade.<br /> <br /> I have toyed with the idea of creating a \u201cSynod of Doctrines\u201d akin to the Council of Traditions or the Union of Conventions. And just as I have a few House rules that provide game system distinctions between science and Magic, I also have some House rules that distinguish system-wise between Magic and faith. And maybe someday, I will post them.<br /> <br /> However, I would not want to see any of that in M5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T15:40:12-07:00","id":1401792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1401785#post1401785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for the sake of speculation, I wanted to know your opinions about dividing the factions, and the ascension war, alongside the three basic ways of understanding magick and the universe: sience, faith and mysticism. I don't remember where I saw this triad, but I always though it would be cool seeing history as a result of the clash between these viewpoints.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at it from a Metaphysical Trinity perspective, it's more like the Trads being Dynamism-biased, the Technos being Stasis-biased, and the Disparates being Primordialism-biased. Then there are two factions of &quot;fallen mages&quot; at the extreme positions of the triangle - Nephandi at Primordialism and Marauders at Dynamism (the Stasis-extremists used to be the Technocracy with the Trads at the centre and the crafts just sort of ... there, but that ended during 2e, leaving there no faction of Stasis-extremism. Maybe Drone Mages, but that relies too heavily on a WTA crossover. IDK.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T17:02:41-07:00","id":1401809,"title":"","content":"In terms of the Science/Faith/Magick triad, I'd never consider the Disparates to be examples of Faith; but otherwise, the associations are decent enough. <br /> <br /> In terms of Nephandi/Marauders/___, note that the first two aren't really factions, per se; they're more like infections. And they don't align with the Metaphysical Trinity so much as they align with the flavors of Quiet: Marauders are literally examples of Madness incarnate; the Nephandi are reasonably close to Morbidity with their \u201cwe must kill Reality\u201d mindset; so the third variety would be Denial-extremism. <br /> <br /> In that regard, the Negation Men (currently classified in the Book of Secrets as a recently emerged Denial-based Marauder variant) could fill that spot. They're essentially the Mage-equivalent of Changeling's extreme-Banality Autumn People, or Mage: the Awakening's Banishers: as written, their extreme \u201cnormality\u201d suppresses all kinds of magick, regardless of what form it takes: they have innate countermagick that disrupts any Effects in their vicinity. <br /> <br /> And <i>that's</i> something that I absolutely would <i>not</i> mind seeing in M5, as a third kind of \u201csickness\u201d alongside the Nephandi and Marauders.<br /> <br /> (For their M5 version, I'd change them slightly: first, the amount of innate countermagick they cause would be tied directly to their level of Denial: the more they are in Denial, the more Countermagick they inflict. Second, I'd take a given Negation Man's Focus into account in deciding whether or not the innate countermagick kicks in, rather than having it always apply.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-08-2020, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T11:23:39-07:00","id":1402969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1401463#post1401463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also... there's the real consideration of IRL factors. WtA is arguably the most overtly political of all the games, bar none - it has a very, VERY clear set of core messages about environmentalism, race, and other factors built into the setting and plot. However, Mage has had political undercurrents as well, but without necessarily always intending it. The naming issue brought up certainly is one, but the more relevant in the modern age (and arguably right now) may be the issues with the Technocrats as objective villains. Not only is this something that's been revisited time and again by the line, but it's something that, given a lot of issues of late, could be something that the game runners wish to avoid - while I doubt the portrayal of the Technocracy is largely or even a little to blame for certain antiscience attitudes in modern culture, it is an issue that may need to be re-examined as we move into a future hypothetical M5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the Technocracy hasn't been &quot;objectively evil&quot; for 20 years - this has even gotten some pushback against it, with folks arguing they've been whitewashed and need to be made darker (I don't agree, given how the new Convention Books haven't exactly glossed over their flaws).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think an issue, though I might be strawmanning here, is will the magick system still be recognizable? V5 presents Disciplines and Sorcery in a manner completely different from the established (and in my opinion, genius) system that came before it. Replacing it with something that might suit someone's tastes better from a mechanical/game design standpoint, but from a lore/metaphyics standpoint they have really gone against the grain.<br /> <br /> What if spheres just become a grouping for related but very specific powers? IE the life sphere's first level comes with a wound healing power, a sickness healing power and a cosmetic power. Potence used to just give you all-around movie-style super-strength , but now it offers hyper-specific strength themed powers per level (Jump high, do more damage to people, do this climbing trick) They function a lot like werewolf gifts now.<br /> Spheres are even more broad than disciplines were. Looking at V5, why wouldn't spheres instead become ten-thousand very specific powers rather than 'I can do anything my spheres say I can do' ? Would you guys welcome this change? </div> </div> </div>If they do that, M5 crashes on takeoff. The core of Mage mechanically and its main selling point is the freeform magic system. Remove that and you'd simultaneously anger the pre-existing fanbase and remove one of its distinguishing features from the other fantasy RPGs already on the market, i.e. what would draw in new fans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1401785#post1401785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for the sake of speculation, I wanted to know your opinions about dividing the factions, and the ascension war, alongside the three basic ways of understanding magick and the universe: sience, faith and mysticism. I don't remember where I saw this triad, but I always though it would be cool seeing history as a result of the clash between these viewpoints.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, all the playable factions have elements of each to an extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 07-15-2020, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T12:05:37-07:00","id":1402972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1402969#post1402969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, the Technocracy hasn't been &quot;objectively evil&quot; for 20 years - this has even gotten some pushback against it, with folks arguing they've been whitewashed and need to be made darker (I don't agree, given how the new Convention Books haven't exactly glossed over their flaws).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If they do that, M5 crashes on takeoff. The core of Mage mechanically and its main selling point is the freeform magic system. Remove that and you'd simultaneously anger the pre-existing fanbase and remove one of its distinguishing features from the other fantasy RPGs already on the market, i.e. what would draw in new fans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, all the playable factions have elements of each to an extent.</div> </div> </div> </div>About the first point the Technocracy began to get friendlier with Technocracy Revised but yeah it whas still evil for a long time before in history and nothing that can be solved in like two decades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T13:16:11-07:00","id":1402978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1402972#post1402972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About the first point the Technocracy began to get friendlier with Technocracy Revised but yeah it whas still evil for a long time before in history and nothing that can be solved in like two decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually even earlier than that. The 2E Guide to the Technocracy definitely cemented the idea of the Technocracy as more than one-note villains but they were going that way before that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T13:57:25-07:00","id":1402981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1402978#post1402978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually even earlier than that. The 2E Guide to the Technocracy definitely cemented the idea of the Technocracy as more than one-note villains but they were going that way before that book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't stop people from arguing that 1e Progenitors and ItX is the gold standard of how they need to be portrayed,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T14:55:12-07:00","id":1402989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1402981#post1402981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't stop people from arguing that 1e Progenitors and ItX is the gold standard of how they need to be portrayed,</div> </div> </div> </div>That's nothing. I've seen people argue that they should be the Alt-Right which is then followed up by me bashing my head against the wall for five minutes to feel something less painful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T15:55:41-07:00","id":1402998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1402989#post1402989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's nothing. I've seen people argue that they should be the Alt-Right which is then followed up by me bashing my head against the wall for five minutes to feel something less painful.</div> </div> </div> </div>See my observation elsewhere about the problem with trying to turn the Technocracy into a stand-in for a real-world political ideology \u2014 especially when that's coupled with \u201cwe can't let them right-winger fans have any fun\u201d (a sentiment that I've actually heard expressed, though not in those words). <br /> <br /> Mage's social commentary works best when it assumes that the players will think about it and come to their own conclusions; the <i>last</i> thing that Mage should be doing is preaching to the reader. Sadly, that's becoming a lost artform these days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T16:22:52-07:00","id":1403001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1401630#post1401630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Rotes, Procedures, and Other Prepared Effects</i> and <i>Knowing and Learning Rotes</i> would go to <i>Step Two: Ability</i>, while <i>Coincidental Magick vs. Vulgar Magick</i> would move to <i>Step One: Effect</i>. Both sections would undergo some changes: I'd at least consider the possibility of replacing the Coincidental vs. Vulgar split with the Subtle/Uncanny/Extreme split that Brucato describes in <b>Mage Made Easy</b>. There <i>would</i> be other changes to the Paradox mechanics; but in Step One, the focus would solely be on deciding how subtle or blatant the Effect is.<br /> <br /> In the <i>Step Two: Ability</i> subsection on Rotes, I would make the controversial decision to add system benefits for knowing a Rote, and an experience point cost for learning one. The fine points would be addressed later; but at this point in the process, the key feature would be that knowing our having access to a Rote can substitute for insufficient levels of Spheres and even Arete. That is, if you don't have enough dots in your Spheres to craft the Effect, but you <i>do</i> have access to the Effect as a Rote, you can still perform it. And if you have access to the Rote, your dice pool is the higher of your Arete or the highest Sphere in the Rote.</div> </div> </div> </div>Allowing rotes to compensate for lower levels of Spheres or Arete seems like making them too powerful. Personally I would just have them reduce the difficulty modifier by -1, but some mechanical effect is necessary.<br /> <br /> I would also crib Arcane Experience from Awakening, reskinning it as Avatar Experience, and make it the XP used to raise Spheres and Arete (this makes failed Seekings less of a total waste).<br /> <br /> Also, unrelated to the magic system, I'd cut down on the grotesque levels of skill bloat. &quot;Energy Weapons&quot; would become Guns (Energy Weapons), &quot;Helmsman&quot; would be Pilot (Spacecraft), etc.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T16:47:23-07:00","id":1403006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1402998#post1402998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See my observation elsewhere about the problem with trying to turn the Technocracy into a stand-in for a real-world political ideology \u2014 especially when that's coupled with \u201cwe can't let them right-winger fans have any fun\u201d (a sentiment that I've actually heard expressed, though not in those words).<br /> <br /> Mage's social commentary works best when it assumes that the players will think about it and come to their own conclusions; the <i>last</i> thing that Mage should be doing is preaching to the reader. Sadly, that's becoming a lost artform these days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree. This is why I said M5 should be about Orphans (without calling them Orphans) and the first sourcebook should be about low lvl and field agents about technocracy so the players see that there no good or bad but different sides.<br /> <br /> This has the Alliance/Horde effect from WoW which is good for two things.<br /> First it let the player thinking and discussing about why exactly their side is right (or legitimate) and what the other side accuses them only propaganda.<br /> Second it increases the sales because you can get fans for both sides that get humored because their side is not the evil guys but only having leadershipproblems","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T16:48:29-07:00","id":1403008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403001#post1403001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allowing rotes to compensate for lower levels of Spheres or Arete seems like making them too powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>did</i> say that it would be a controversial decision. That said, let me point out that M20 already lets you do nearly the same thing that I'm proposing through the Enhancements Background: gain access to a single Rote independent of your Arete and Spheres. The rationale is different (for an Enhancement, it takes the form of incorporating a Device into yourself), but the result is similar enough that I question the notion that allowing Rotes to compensate for lower levels of Spheres or Arete makes them too powerful. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403001#post1403001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also crib Arcane Experience from Awakening, reskinning it as Avatar Experience, and make it the XP used to raise Spheres and Arete (this makes failed Seekings less of a total waste).</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed. It would also potentially give some teeth to your choice of Essence, on the theory that your Avatar Essence would factor into how you earn Avatar Experience. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403001#post1403001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, unrelated to the magic system, I'd cut down on the grotesque levels of skill bloat. &quot;Energy Weapons&quot; would become Guns (Energy Weapons), &quot;Helmsman&quot; would be Pilot (Spacecraft), etc.</div> </div> </div> </div> Also agreed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T21:35:01-07:00","id":1403040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1402998#post1402998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See my observation elsewhere about the problem with trying to turn the Technocracy into a stand-in for a real-world political ideology \u2014 especially when that's coupled with \u201cwe can't let them right-winger fans have any fun\u201d (a sentiment that I've actually heard expressed, though not in those words).<br /> <br /> Mage's social commentary works best when it assumes that the players will think about it and come to their own conclusions; the <i>last</i> thing that Mage should be doing is preaching to the reader. Sadly, that's becoming a lost artform these days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, unfortunately I once got in a rather heated argument with a couple of MtAs newcomers at a gaming store who were utterly convinced that the Technocracy were nothing more than Alt-Right Fascists that sought to enslave the minds and souls of everyone and were actually <i>worse </i>than the Nephandi because they also believed the BS that Nephandi wish to destroy the shitty WoD so a better world could be born from the ashes. (Because of course they would.) I think they got their information for poor Internet research and that MtAs text game that was released alongside the VtM We Eat Blood that supposedly painted the Technocracy as Alt-Right which doesn't surprise me given what I heard about We Eat Blood. Actually probably more the latter as they at one point started talking about the Union hating and fearing non-whites because non-whites are more 'spiritually-open' or some such nonsense that frankly comes across as racist itself.<br /> <br /> The sad thing too was that I had been having a nice conversation with them up to that point about MtAs and then I mention I was attempting to put together a Technocracy game and asked if they wanted to join to get a chance to play MtAs. The moment I said that, they looked at me like I asked them if they wanted to help me murder someone and went completely nuts on me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T04:19:49-07:00","id":1403081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403040#post1403040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they got their information for poor Internet research and that MtAs text game that was released alongside the VtM We Eat Blood that supposedly painted the Technocracy as Alt-Right which doesn't surprise me given what I heard about We Eat Blood. Actually probably more the latter as they at one point started talking about the Union hating and fearing non-whites because non-whites are more 'spiritually-open' or some such nonsense that frankly comes across as racist itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I played Mage Refugee. It is true, that it paint the Technocracy Xenophob where they want to keep Refugess out because they are bringing their own superstitions and so bring people further from the rational thinking. Though I agree that it paint the Technocracy unnececary evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T06:30:20-07:00","id":1403090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403081#post1403081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I played Mage Refugee. It is true, that it paint the Technocracy Xenophob where they want to keep Refugess out because they are bringing their own superstitions and so bring people further from the rational thinking. Though I agree that it paint the Technocracy unnececary evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I was right... Okay, screw both those games now. I thought just We Eat Blood was bad but now I that indeed Refugee wasn't much better. Truly they were warning signs for the mess that was to come.<br /> <br /> Though I will admit that it was amusing seeing them react to the fact that the SoE and VA were Technocrats originally because they were so crazy that they refused to even admit that the Technocrats were Awakened as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T07:23:38-07:00","id":1403094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403090#post1403090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I was right... Okay, screw both those games now. I thought just We Eat Blood was bad but now I that indeed Refugee wasn't much better. Truly they were warning signs for the mess that was to come.<br /> <br /> Though I will admit that it was amusing seeing them react to the fact that the SoE and VA were Technocrats originally because they were so crazy that they refused to even admit that the Technocrats were Awakened as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>They must not have read the corebook or even the wiki. There's ignorance and there's ... that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's nothing. I've seen people argue that they should be the Alt-Right which is then followed up by me bashing my head against the wall for five minutes to feel something less painful. </div> </div> </div>On the opposite side of things, I saw somebody recently argue on another site that the Traditions should be turned into alt-right conspiracy theorists and the Technocracy whitewashed to the point of absurdity. Like, the stuff that goes on in Room 101 is now literally just mundane cult deprogramming techniques. To which I really have no words other than &quot;WTF?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 07-16-2020, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T09:49:20-07:00","id":1403109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403094#post1403094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those guys must not have read the corebook or even the wiki. There's ignorance and there's ... that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a guy and a girl actually. And honestly looking back at it I should have figured it as they were kind of hippie-ish and were especially gushing over how awesome the various Tradition beliefs were, namely the Dreamspeakers, Verebena and CoX were (maybe some others I can't remember beyond that the OoH, SoE and VA weren't among them). The warning signs were there but I didn't quite see it.<br /> <br /> But at the end I start paraphrasing part of the introduction of Guide to the Technocracy at them. The fancy cellphone you got? That's the Technocracy. You're welcome. That car you drove here in? That's the Technocracy. You're welcome. The printing machines that created the books you're holding? That's the Technocracy. You're welcome.<br /> <br /> After that they gave me the stink eye and wandered off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403094#post1403094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the opposite side of things, I saw somebody recently argue on another site that the Traditions should be turned into alt-right conspiracy theorists and the Technocracy whitewashed to the point of absurdity. Like, the stuff that goes on in Room 101 is now literally just mundane cult deprogramming techniques. To which I really have no words other than &quot;WTF?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... my thoughts exactly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T11:13:43-07:00","id":1403124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403094#post1403094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the opposite side of things, I saw somebody recently argue on another site that the Traditions should be turned into alt-right conspiracy theorists and the Technocracy whitewashed to the point of absurdity. Like, the stuff that goes on in Room 101 is now literally just mundane cult deprogramming techniques. To which I really have no words other than &quot;WTF?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I'm working on something for Navalon, playing up the concept as presented in M20 (they've left the Technocracy because they can't stand how corrupt it's become), and I find myself wanting to portray them as a reaction to the Technocracy's \u201ccontrol freak\u201d tendencies (or, put another way, its tendency to think that it's knows what's good for you more than you do). But at the same time, I don't want to push them into the same territory that Czernobog is describing here. If Navalon reforms Room 101 into cult deprogramming, for instance, and plays its counter to the NWO as being devoted to promoting \u201cresponsible citizenship\u201d where the Masses are to be taught enough about the real nature of the world to empower them to make informed decisions for themselves instead of relying on a shadowy organization of technocrats (lower-case, real-world definition of the term) to do it for them, what are the unintended consequences? Other than \u201clingering technocratic tendencies\u201d, which <i>would</i> still be a problem, but isn't really what I'm looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-21-2020, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T12:24:04-07:00","id":1403141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403124#post1403124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I'm working on something for Navalon, playing up the concept as presented in M20 (they've left the Technocracy because they can't stand how corrupt it's become), and I find myself wanting to portray them as a reaction to the Technocracy's \u201ccontrol freak\u201d tendencies (or, put another way, its tendency to think that it's knows what's good for you more than you do). But at the same time, I don't want to push them into the same territory that Czernobog is describing here. If Navalon reforms Room 101 into cult deprogramming, for instance, and plays its counter to the NWO as being devoted to promoting \u201cresponsible citizenship\u201d where the Masses are too be taught enough about the real nature of the world to empower them to make informed decisions for themselves instead of relying on a shadowy organization of technocrats (lower-case, real-world definition of the term) to do it for them, what are the unintended consequences? Other than \u201clingering technocratic tendencies\u201d, which <i>would</i> still be a problem, but isn't really what I'm looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>That bizarre idea was essentially simply demonising the Traditions and glorifying the Technocracy in an inversion of 1e, I wouldn't take it too seriously.<br /> <br /> Personally I don't really like Navalon as a concept, largely because the name sounds like a brand of prescription medicine and having them essentially as just another Disparate Craft seems to be a waste. My own version of the idea has them as essentially the more reasonable/pragmatic view of the Technocracy as presented in Revised - essentially treading the line between &quot;Dark Guardians&quot; and &quot;Reasonably Enlightened&quot; from that old &quot;Calibrating Ascension War Factions&quot; thread (with the TU under Threat Null being Dreamslayers), and with the VAs and Etherites added to give room for the Batini and Solificati to rejoin the Traditions. But I certainly wouldn't go so far as to completely remove their flaws like CB: ItX did - many of them are still in favor of turning the Ascension War back on once this whole Threat Null problem is sorted out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 07-16-2020, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T05:53:13-07:00","id":1403648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1401463#post1401463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that W5 is going in a direction that seems to line up with, or at least is parallel to, the setting established in the LARP rules, and given the trailers we've seen, the old divisions/subsplats for Werewolves likely still exist as clans still exist for vampires, so I doubt the traditions will go anywhere, but they definitely will be suffering in the wake of the Second Inquisition (possibly less than Vampires, though).</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue with playing up the SI for M5 is that it's pretty much a weaksauce version of what was going on in 1e and 2e. They don't have combat cyborgs, bio-engineered war-creatures, Umbral spaceships that can steal your node from under you etc. Unless they're Technocratic cat's-paws, in which case why not have the Technocracy directly fighting the Traditions like in 1e and 2e?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T10:27:42-07:00","id":1403684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403648#post1403648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with playing up the SI for M5 is that it's pretty much a weaksauce version of what was going on in 1e and 2e. They don't have combat cyborgs, bio-engineered war-creatures, Umbral spaceships that can steal your node from under you etc. Unless they're Technocratic cat's-paws, in which case why not have the Technocracy directly fighting the Traditions like in 1e and 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d further note that the Second Inquisition probably wouldn\u2019t even recognize 80% of modern magic as magic.<br /> <br /> Are they going to hunt down Tibetan monks for following their religious practices? How about Christian revivalists? New Age sensualists? Kooky inventors? Wiccan groups on college campuses? Computer hackers?<br /> <br /> Maybe they manage to identify some Euthanatos, but not for their magic (leveraging karma isn\u2019t really all that distinguishable from general spirtualism and luck) but because they kill things that are also targets of the Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> About the only ones practicing what the groups comprising the Second Inquisition would recognize as magic are the Order of Hermes and Hollow Ones and you\u2019ve got yourself a bear of a time telling the real ones apart from all those who joined some Hermetic Order of the Golden Dawn as a social club not much different than the Masons.<br /> <br /> Vampires and, to a lesser extent, werewolves are good targets for the Second Inquisition because they\u2019re clearly inhuman beings... vampires even show up on conventional detection equipment (i.e. thermal imaging).<br /> <br /> Mages though are humans with human families and embedded in human organizations and often affiliated with minority religious groups. How do you sell targeting a group of Kabbalist Rabbis in New York City or an indigenous people\u2019s rights group or a Wiccan club at the University of Chicago without looking like some sort of terror organization?<br /> <br /> And for what crime? Are the Second Inquisition going to blow up an indigenous rights group for holding religious services they believe can help sway others to their cause? Are they going to assassinate a New Age fortune teller in LA for holding seances to get stock tips?<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition simply cannot be a credible threat to Mage society because their targets aren\u2019t doing anything the SI groups could recognize as a threat to organize a hunt against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T11:10:20-07:00","id":1403689,"title":"","content":"Indeed. The fact of the matter is that MtAs has had little in the way of pure human Hunters, partly because it's extremely difficult to tell a Mage apart from an ordinary human. With vampires, you can put on thermal googles and find vampires in a crowd pretty quickly. But how can you tell a Mage apart from a Sorcerer or just an ordinary person playing with vaguely occult nicknacks?<br /> <br /> And then there's the Technocracy which would be so out of the SI's league that they couldn't hope to take them on.<br /> <br /> What makes the SI terrifying for vampires is that vampires aren't as terrifying in the modern world. Modern technology and weapons have made things more even on the playing field.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T11:18:10-07:00","id":1403691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403684#post1403684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the only ones practicing what the groups comprising the Second Inquisition would recognize as magic are the Order of Hermes and Hollow Ones and you\u2019ve got yourself a bear of a time telling the real ones apart from all those who joined some Hermetic Order of the Golden Dawn as a social club not much different than the Masons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just make it Hermetics - Hollow Ones would largely appear as scene kids and Goths hanging out in nightclubs to the SI.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe they manage to identify some Euthanatos, but not for their magic (leveraging karma isn\u2019t really all that distinguishable from general spirtualism and luck) but because they kill things that are also targets of the Second Inquisition. </div> </div> </div>In which case &quot;weirdly lucky superstitious peeps who also hunt vampires&quot; would probably seem more like potential allies from the SI's POV.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Indeed. The fact of the matter is that MtAs has had little in the way of pure human Hunters, partly because it's extremely difficult to tell a Mage apart from an ordinary human. With vampires, you can put on thermal googles and find vampires in a crowd pretty quickly. But how can you tell a Mage apart from a Sorcerer or just an ordinary person playing with vaguely occult nicknacks?<br /> <br /> And then there's the Technocracy which would be so out of the SI's league that they couldn't hope to take them on.<br /> <br /> What makes the SI terrifying for vampires is that vampires aren't as terrifying in the modern world. Modern technology and weapons have made things more even on the playing field. </div> </div> </div>Yes, the only way the SI work as a threat to the Traditions is as cat's-paws of the Technocracy ... in which case, why not just restart the Ascension War?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 07-20-2020, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T12:14:21-07:00","id":1403696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403691#post1403691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... in which case, why not just restart the Ascension War?</div> </div> </div> </div>to avoid a resurgence of those 'technocracy vs traditions' threads","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T13:05:56-07:00","id":1403702,"title":"","content":"I don't have a problem with that \u2014 as long as all sides involved (except perhaps the Nephandi) have valid points to make, and it doesn't devolve to \u201cmagic good, science bad!\u201d<br /> <br /> And in all honesty, I really don't see that pitfall happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T18:27:34-07:00","id":1403734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403691#post1403691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just make it Hermetics - Hollow Ones would largely appear as scene kids and Goths hanging out in nightclubs to the SI.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking the serious Victorian occultists like Crowley (a Hollow One per Mage lore) rather than the more modern pop-occultists.<br /> <br /> But the same is also true with the Hermetics. Only the hopelessly out of date are wearing robes and chanting Latin in the basement. The modern Hermetic is a lifetime member of some \u201cOld Boys\u201d Club like the Skull &amp; Bones and is just as powerful pulling out their cell phone and running down their contact list as they are when they destroy someone financially by summoning up an electricity elemental from a magic circle of seven rune inscribed credit cards and sending it forth to shift every digital one-and-zero of their enemy\u2019s bank accounts to various charities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In which case &amp;quot;weirdly lucky superstitious peeps who also hunt vampires&amp;quot; would probably seem more like potential allies from the SI's POV. </div> </div> </div>No disagreements here either... and yet ANOTHER reason why the Second Inquisition as a Mage antagonist is a non-starter; too many Mages would be on the same side as the SI against the vampires.<br /> <br /> The Euthanatos are just one example. The conflict between the Order of Hermes and Clan Tremere was legendary enough to get its own Mage book. Vampirism is antithetical to the beliefs of just about every Tradition and only \u201cwe\u2019ve got bigger fish to fry\u201d keeps the Technocratic \u201cWe killed an Antideluvean\u201d Union from making the Second Inquisition look like Amateur Hour.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, the only way the SI work as a threat to the Traditions is as cat's-paws of the Technocracy ... in which case, why not just restart the Ascension War? </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think they even work as a cat\u2019s paw; the other reason why the Technocracy doesn\u2019t go after the vampires is because they largely self-police and preserve the status quo. Sending a half-assed effort like the SI would just rile things up and make the status quo harder to maintain.<br /> <br /> Similarly, sending the SI at Tradition Mages is basically a backfire waiting to happen. The sort of operations the SI conducts leveled at human religious groups is a sure fire way to win sympathy and interest for groups the Technocracy would rather see marginalized until they\u2019re forgotten and fade to nothingness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T18:41:00-07:00","id":1403736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403734#post1403734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t think they even work as a cat\u2019s paw; the other reason why the Technocracy doesn\u2019t go after the vampires is because they largely self-police and preserve the status quo. Sending a half-assed effort like the SI would just rile things up and make the status quo harder to maintain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean ItX, the Progenitors and the VEs are pretty eager to get in on hunting vampires. But the guys who set the Union's political agenda and supply the funds (both mundane and quint) don't care because, as you said, vamps largely self-police. So anything is largely gonna be done by local Amalgams, not as a Union-wide policy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T20:43:38-07:00","id":1403752,"title":"","content":"I'll have to disagree about Iteration X and the Void Engineers: the latter generally aren't around Earth's cities often enough to have any real awareness of the problem, and the former only really concern themselves with vampires to the extent that the leeches interfere with the smooth operation of society \u2014 which, as long as the Kindred keep their heads down and stay in the shadows, is minimal. <br /> <br /> Only the Progenitors strike me as the type to react to vampires with \u201cthey must be destroyed!\u201d, as the undead are anathema to the Convention's focus on life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T02:05:43-07:00","id":1403781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403752#post1403752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only the Progenitors strike me as the type to react to vampires with \u201cthey must be destroyed!\u201d, as the undead are anathema to the Convention's focus on life.</div> </div> </div> </div>but are they the ones doing the destroying?<br /> iirc, the toasters are the ones tasked with the hunting<br /> <br /> thing is, I don't think it matters whether or not hunting vampires or whatever is logical or approaved by this or that convention,<br /> what matters is that, if we're making the technocracy playable, they're gonna need a target<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T03:35:07-07:00","id":1403791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403684#post1403684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d further note that the Second Inquisition probably wouldn\u2019t even recognize 80% of modern magic as magic.<br /> <br /> Are they going to hunt down Tibetan monks for following their religious practices? How about Christian revivalists? New Age sensualists? Kooky inventors? Wiccan groups on college campuses? Computer hackers?<br /> <br /> Maybe they manage to identify some Euthanatos, but not for their magic (leveraging karma isn\u2019t really all that distinguishable from general spirtualism and luck) but because they kill things that are also targets of the Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> About the only ones practicing what the groups comprising the Second Inquisition would recognize as magic are the Order of Hermes and Hollow Ones and you\u2019ve got yourself a bear of a time telling the real ones apart from all those who joined some Hermetic Order of the Golden Dawn as a social club not much different than the Masons.<br /> <br /> Vampires and, to a lesser extent, werewolves are good targets for the Second Inquisition because they\u2019re clearly inhuman beings... vampires even show up on conventional detection equipment (i.e. thermal imaging).<br /> <br /> Mages though are humans with human families and embedded in human organizations and often affiliated with minority religious groups. How do you sell targeting a group of Kabbalist Rabbis in New York City or an indigenous people\u2019s rights group or a Wiccan club at the University of Chicago without looking like some sort of terror organization?<br /> <br /> And for what crime? Are the Second Inquisition going to blow up an indigenous rights group for holding religious services they believe can help sway others to their cause? Are they going to assassinate a New Age fortune teller in LA for holding seances to get stock tips?<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition simply cannot be a credible threat to Mage society because their targets aren\u2019t doing anything the SI groups could recognize as a threat to organize a hunt against.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree. Those who they can target are the wunderheiler though those are normally targeted because they are fraudulent. But when it really work and you do not advertise you as a licenced medican but just one with gifted hands and send the people that are over your league to mundane docters you are safe from the SI. The Technocracy on the other side is another topic which you will get soon on your ass if you are to succesfull because if you are not a mage you are a sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Though would the SI even be in the hands of the Technocracy? Would it not be rather the traditions? I mean dataanalytic is the specialization of the Mercurian Elite, the celestial chorus and the refugees from templers would concentrate on the spiritual support and the order of hermes, that believes like the SI (or believe the SI because of the Order) that the Blood Mages are the rulers of the vampires,would rather love to take care of the tremere while the sons of ether would suply the SI with modern weaponary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 07-21-2020, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T05:19:05-07:00","id":1403795,"title":"","content":"I mean, the SI are a collection of secret factions within various intelligence services. They wouldn't really be interested in homeopaths, acupuncture practitioners or faith healers as threats to organise hunts against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T07:00:44-07:00","id":1403802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403795#post1403795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the SI are a collection of secret factions within various intelligence services. They wouldn't really be interested in homeopaths, acupuncture practitioners or faith healers as threats to organise hunts against.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah this is why I said you would be safe from SI but not from the Technocracy where especially the progenitors would want to eliminate you for not being part of the Schoolmedicine.<br /> Though mayby you would be as a faithhealer not so safe from the SI because they want to recruit you for this cause mayby even with force because you are so much worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T08:00:52-07:00","id":1403815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403781#post1403781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> but are they the ones doing the destroying?<br /> iirc, the toasters are the ones tasked with the hunting<br /> <br /> thing is, I don't think it matters whether or not hunting vampires or whatever is logical or approaved by this or that convention,<br /> what matters is that, if we're making the technocracy playable, they're gonna need a target</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>have</i> targets. First, there's the old standby of Superstitionists. If you want them to be a bit more palatable, just have them be a bit more discerning and focus more on \u201cthe Superstitionists who are actually causing problems\u201d: the Book of Shadows had a story in it (which I think was the first appearance of John Courage?) featuring a NWO agent taking down a Cultist of Ecstasy who had been reseating dangerous drugs onto the streets. Second, the Union can go after Nephandi and Marauders. <br /> <br /> But also: according to Technocracy Reloaded, while the Union generally takes a hands off policy with respect to vampires, they tend to be rather aggressive where werewolves are concerned. <br /> <br /> But finally, the Union does more than just hunt. While that's generally all that matters about them when your chronicle is centered around those groups that they <i>do</i> hunt, a Technocracy-centered chronicle might never involve that side of things. Instead, the Conventions each have their own goals that they pursue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T08:58:04-07:00","id":1403822,"title":"","content":"After reading a lot of your thoughts, I wonder if reality itself should be the &quot;SI&quot; of an eventual M5. <br /> I remember that Jess Hening, the MRev developper, once said something in the line of : yes, an AK-47 does more damage than a Force3 Prime 2 spell, but that's the point : mages should <b>choose </b>to do magic.&quot; It is something that could be easily adapted to an eventual M5, especialy since we don't know what are Paradox plans to do with the timeline. Make that Avatar Storm still a thing, or just don't follow on M20 timeline neutral-ish, and you have a justification on why magic(k) is still hard. It also could be used to justify the Technocracy's role as an antagonist, since it doesn't do &quot;magic&quot;. <br /> <br /> Also, it could be a way to distinguish M5 form M20, the same way there was a clear intention to differentiate V5 from V20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2140-asimar","name":"Asimar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T09:30:29-07:00","id":1403825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403815#post1403815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They <i>have</i> targets. First, there's the old standby of Superstitionists. If you want them to be a bit more palatable, just have them be a bit more discerning and focus more on \u201cthe Superstitionists who are actually causing problems\u201d: the Book of Shadows had a story in it (which I think was the first appearance of John Courage?) featuring a NWO agent taking down a Cultist of Ecstasy who had been reseating dangerous drugs onto the streets. Second, the Union can go after Nephandi and Marauders.<br /> <br /> But also: according to Technocracy Reloaded, while the Union generally takes a hands off policy with respect to vampires, they tend to be rather aggressive where werewolves are concerned.<br /> <br /> But finally, the Union does more than just hunt. While that's generally all that matters about them when your chronicle is centered around those groups that they <i>do</i> hunt, a Technocracy-centered chronicle might never involve that side of things. Instead, the Conventions each have their own goals that they pursue.</div> </div> </div> </div>echoing the complaints I've heard from Mage players, marauders/nephandi are not popular antagonists (especially naphandi)<br /> <br /> Mages are not very numerous,<br /> hunting or not hunting, they don't offer a steady source of conflict,<br /> which got even worse after the techies got made into good guys, making it more difficult to introduce or justify hostilities<br /> <br /> compare that to VtM or WtA where the setting pretty much harasses you with conflict...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T09:40:59-07:00","id":1403828,"title":"","content":"I'm sure I read an older version of V5 that had good left-wing brujah contrasted with evil right wing brujah types... well, that's not in whatever iteration i'm currently reading, but the current book still has a good deal of preaching elsewhere.<br /> <br /> There are right wing Traditions and left wing traditions; the same is true for Technocrats. Etherites don't imagine themselves getting the funding they need for their research from the state and thus need big private capital to get their projects off the ground, and with Hermetics we know they love money and we all think of secret societies where members help each other out when we think of them, but whether they're into glorious imagined pasts and strong state control or deregulation and small government... really depends on the hermetic house or the individual in question. The Virtual Adepts are undoubtedly on both sides: Silicon valley makes a lot of money, but the internet is by it's very nature a space of communal effort.... ...and while the romantic image of the Shaman or Witch is one of the poor, is that really grounded in reality?<br /> <br /> The traditions are politically all over the place. I think, maybe, they could get it right after a few edits. The issue is that they're probably going to overemphasize nephandi as Nazis<br /> <br /> <br /> RE Mages and the SI<br /> <br /> The SI is logistically impossible unless it's either exaggerated and really just a cover for vampires to kill eachother or it's all the work of mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-21-2020, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T10:06:58-07:00","id":1403834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403752#post1403752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to disagree about Iteration X and the Void Engineers: the latter generally aren't around Earth's cities often enough to have any real awareness of the problem,</div> </div> </div> </div>The VEs used not to care. Then the Week of Nightmares happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and the former only really concern themselves with vampires to the extent that the leeches interfere with the smooth operation of society \u2014 which, as long as the Kindred keep their heads down and stay in the shadows, is minimal. </div> </div> </div>Ironically ItX in their 1e incarnation were pals with the Sabbat - though that whole book has been retconned to be a piece of Etherite propaganda, so it doesn't really count.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this whole thing has been something of a derail and I'd like to get it back on track.<br /> <br /> Speaking about rotes - IMO they should definitely be more than a fluff thing, but allowing players to use them to transcend their arete and sphere dots seems a bit too strong (especially as Devices need to be charged with Quint and Enhancements both need to be charged and come with permadox). I think something more similar to Awakening's take on rotes might work - play it as the various groups' respective magical styles digging &quot;grooves&quot; into reality similar to Mythic Threads which make those specific uses of the spheres easier.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T11:35:37-07:00","id":1403851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403825#post1403825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> echoing the complaints I've heard from Mage players, marauders/nephandi are not popular antagonists (especially naphandi)<br /> <br /> Mages are not very numerous,<br /> hunting or not hunting, they don't offer a steady source of conflict,<br /> which got even worse after the techies got made into good guys, making it more difficult to introduce or justify hostilities<br /> <br /> compare that to VtM or WtA where the setting pretty much harasses you with conflict...</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is what I tried to solve with my new division of the various factions. Here's the hypothetical metaplot behind it:<br /> <br /> -Avatar Storm breaks in 2015, though &quot;Avatar winds&quot; still show up from time to time in localised areas, complicating cross-Gauntlet travel as ST deems appropriate.<br /> -Technocracy begins to recolonise Umbra, encounters Threat Null. Leadership of Conventions largely subverted.<br /> -Forewarned, large groups of more idealistic Technocrats (and the whole VE Convention) manage to escape Threat Null's attempted purge, form NOR.<br /> -Technocracy restarts war on Traditions, radicalising younger mages who now feel the NHC's acknowledgement of the Technoparadigm's dominance was a pointless display of subservience. They rally around &quot;reality terrorists&quot; who never stopped fighting since the 90s and the spiritised archmasters and masters, forming the Rogue Council.<br /> -Disparates reveal themselves as third major faction, adopt position of armed neutrality.<br /> -VAs and Etherites split - many join NOR while more mystically enclined ones join the mystical Traditions, increasing the numbers of technomages, some even flip out and join the RC. Solificati and Ahl-i-Batin reclaim the Seats of Correspondence and Matter.<br /> -Marauders go about Marauding as always, Nephandi take advantage of the distraction of the major factions to step up recruitment, cause trouble where they can, and put forward longer-term plans ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 07-21-2020, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T12:36:57-07:00","id":1403862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403851#post1403851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is what I tried to solve with my new division of the various factions. Here's the hypothetical metaplot behind it:<br /> <br /> -Avatar Storm breaks in 2015, though &quot;Avatar winds&quot; still show up from time to time in localised areas, complicating cross-Gauntlet travel as ST deems appropriate.<br /> -Technocracy begins to recolonise Umbra, encounters Threat Null. Leadership of Conventions largely subverted.<br /> -Forewarned, large groups of more idealistic Technocrats (and the whole VE Convention) manage to escape Threat Null's attempted purge, form NOR.<br /> -Technocracy restarts war on Traditions, radicalising younger mages who feel the NHC's acknowledgement of the Technoparadigm's dominance was a pointless display of subservience. They rally around &quot;reality terrorists&quot; who never stopped fighting since the 90s and the spiritised archmasters and masters, forming the Rogue Council.<br /> -Disparates reveal themselves as third major faction, adopt position of armed neutrality.<br /> -VAs and Etherites split - many join NOR while more mystically enclined ones join the mystical Traditions, increasing the numbers of technomages, or even flip our and join the RC. Solificati and Ahl-i-Batin reclaim the Seats of Correspondence and Matter.<br /> -Marauders go about Marauding as always, Nephandi take advantage of the distraction of the major factions to step up recruitment, cause trouble where they can, and put forward longer-term plans ...</div> </div> </div> </div>that's a good step to reintroduce conflict,<br /> but it still doesn't solve the lack of numbers<br /> <br /> mages are not very numerous and people don't awaken at a fast pace,<br /> <br /> a possible fix would be to involve hedge-magicians, not just as side characters but more involved with Awakened conflicts and politics<br /> <br /> another fix would be to introduce crossover elements such as hunters or the Possessed from WtA (Fomori, drones etc)<br /> <br /> werewolves, fera and vampires can be used too (if you can solve the werewolf reproduction problem and rebalance the nightfolk countermagic rules)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T12:42:53-07:00","id":1403864,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a> can you please define more how the fera reproduction is is a problem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T12:53:21-07:00","id":1403868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403862#post1403862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> that's a good step to reintroduce conflict,<br /> but it still doesn't solve the lack of numbers<br /> <br /> mages are not very numerous and people don't awaken at a fast pace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages are about 1 in 150,000, which with the current world population gives us a total of 50,000. In comparison vamps are about 75,000, which is only half again as much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 07-21-2020, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T12:57:21-07:00","id":1403869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403864#post1403864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> can you please define more how the fera reproduction is is a problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>werewolves can only reproduce with either humans or wolves, <br /> the offspring has a rather small chance of being a werewolf,<br /> <br /> add to that the rate at which werewolves get killed by their enemies and one of the main threats garou are facing is extinction <br /> <br /> other fera don't necessarily share that fate, <br /> wererats, for example, don't lack numbers (if I remember correctly)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T13:04:17-07:00","id":1403870,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I really like infernalism. Can we make infernalism great again? They make great enemies, and I rather liked the </span></span></span><i>Bartimaeus </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">trilogy as a kid and the dynamic struggles between magician master and bound demon slave. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403864#post1403864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a> can you please define more how the fera reproduction is is a problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the exception of our glorious rat underlords, Fera have always been on the decline. They get killed more than they reproduce, and reproducing as much as they need to has severe ethical implications and isn't sustainable. Ratkin are a nuclear option. <br /> <br /> <br /> Vampires, infernalists and Formori, to my knowledge, are the only &quot;viable&quot; fast productions (and you really shouldn't...). Hedge wizards and their techno counterparts would also work if their production began large scale, but if they could just do that they would've done so already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T13:04:32-07:00","id":1403871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403868#post1403868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mages are about 1 in 150,000, which with the current population gives us a total of 50,000. In comparison vamps are about 75,000, which is only half again as much.</div> </div> </div> </div>that could work, <br /> but how many in a large city like new york?<br /> <br /> the thing with vampires is that their numbers tend to go over the 1 in 100 000 <br /> <br /> in some city by night books, the named npcs go over the ratio","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T13:12:02-07:00","id":1403873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403869#post1403869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> werewolves can only reproduce with either humans or wolves,<br /> the offspring has a rather small chance of being a werewolf,<br /> <br /> add to that the rate at which werewolves get killed by their enemies and one of the main threats garou are facing is extinction<br /> <br /> other fera don't necessarily share that fate,<br /> wererats, for example, don't lack numbers (if I remember correctly)</div> </div> </div> </div>That is because Ratkin still have the luxus that garou do not have, Ratkin can produce en masse with ratkinfolk. For garou most of the lupus kinfolk is dead so they have no real way to massbread anymore except they are trying the same as the BSD to breed Metis. Though I think this will clearly not be solved this way because it would be way to political dangerous to state, that to prevent extinction it is expected for every female garou, that is pregnant from a lupuskinfolk to breed with another garou to birth as many metis as possible to have canonfood because with Metis being sterile it is no big deal if they will die for the planet. The other problem is, that this plan would definataly bring the Black furies against the nation because their pride will not allow something like this. So unless they make Garou way more op from nothing, make Metis not sterile anymore or just let suddenly many wolves appear out of nothing the setting is bound to be fucked because the fera are lacking way with numbers.<br /> <br /> But yeah nearly all Fera except Corax, Ananasi and Ratkin have the numberproblem.<br /> Corax because they are the only Fera, which have no need for kinfolk for reproduction, they can make sure, that a corax will born from the species the corax is not born from.<br /> Ananasi because they are the other fera, that have like Ratkin the Luxus of big numbers of their kinfolk to breed to.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T13:16:19-07:00","id":1403875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403870#post1403870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I really like infernalism. Can we make infernalism great again? They make great enemies, and I rather liked the </span></span></span><i>Bartimaeus </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">trilogy as a kid and the dynamic struggles between magician master and bound demon slave. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I liked Bartimaeus too, but the beings there aren't really demonic - it's more like a Hermetic Victory world than an Infernalist victory one.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T14:26:46-07:00","id":1403886,"title":"","content":"It's not hard to imagine a darker take on the setting though... <br /> <br /> But also, straddling the line with evil and struggling with yourself and external factors as you cling to control knowing that to lose it would mean your destruction... <br /> <br /> yeah, maybe I just want em more mainstream... The more prominent they are, the better the treatment they get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T20:04:58-07:00","id":1403930,"title":"","content":"On the Void Engineers: yes, the Week of Nightmares happened. And then the Dimensional Anomaly happened, the Void Engineers were decimated, Threat Null appeared along with an onslaught by Umbrood, and concerns about what's happening on Earth were once again on the back burner. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403834#post1403834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking about rotes - IMO they should definitely be more than a fluff thing, but allowing players to use them to transcend their arete and sphere dots seems a bit too strong (especially as Devices need to be charged with Quint and Enhancements both need to be charged and come with permadox).</div> </div> </div> </div> the idea I'm working with is that Rotes would need to be \u201ccharged\u201d with XP instead of Quint (and would take longer to acquire), and that the Permadox/Genetic Flaws that Enhancements have come from them being an unnatural distortion of the subject's Pattern; Rotes aren't. Though I wouldn't be against the notion that performing an Effect by Rote is actually disadvantaged in some way if you don't have sufficient Spheres or Arete to back it up. <br /> <br /> But the real reason behind my suggestion is that it enables formalizing the hack that appeared in <b>Gods &amp; Monsters</b> for Hedge Magicians: rather than handling Hedge Magic as a separate magic system that requires a page count comparable to the Sphere Magic system, you can handle Sleeper Magic using an extension to the Awakened Magick system that takes up maybe an additional page or two; and Rotes that transcend Arete and Sphere limits are central to that. <br /> <br /> And that also factors into the suggestion of making Hedge Magicians a bigger part of the setting: you <i>can't do that</i> if you have to essentially double the page count devoted to magic to present separate Sleeper and Awakened systems; we're <i>already</i> having to make space-saving considerations such as whether or not to devote space to Tradition/Convention/Craft write-ups in the core book or to put the bulk of that material in a supplement and focus on independent mages in the core book. When those are the sorts of decisions under consideration, two separate magic system's in the core book is a non-starter. <br /> <br /> So if you want to pick up on the \u201cRise of the Extraordinary Citizen\u201d metaplot idea introduced in the Revised NWO Convention Book (i.e., \u201cever since the Dimensional Anomaly rolled around, the number of Extraordinary Citizens has spiked; and nobody knows why\u201d), you're going to need something like what I'm describing. <br /> <br /> And conceptually, I much prefer the notion of Sleeper Magic as a subset of Awakened Magick: that is, the Sleeper magicians have a Focus (Paradigm, Practice, and Instruments) just like the Awakened do; but because the Sleeper magicians don't have Arete or Spheres, the <i>only way</i> they can practice magic is by Rote. <br /> <br /> If you still want Sorcerers who use Hedge Magic Paths in your games, you can publish a <b>Sorcerer II</b> book that goes back to <b>World of Darkness: Sorcerer</b>'s notion that Hedge Magic is a distinct phenomenon from Awakened Magick, with the added twist that it's also distinct from the Sleeper Magic that would be featured in M5. This new edition of Sorcerer would exist to provide the <i>rest</i> of the World of Darkness with magicians without using <b>Mage</b> to do so. In that book, I would have mages explicitly recognize that Hedge Magic is no more related to Sphere Magick than vampiric Disciplines are. I wouldn't even publish the book as a M5 supplement; it would be a generic World of Darkness book in much the same way the original <b>Sorcerer</b> was. <br /> <br /> And as such, it wouldn't really be relevant to M5. For M5, I'd insist that Hedge Magic never even gets referenced; just use the \u201cMagic by Rote\u201d option to handle acolytes and extraordinary citizens who actually know a trick or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T17:45:44-07:00","id":1404326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403930#post1403930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea I'm working with is that Rotes would need to be \u201ccharged\u201d with XP instead of Quint (and would take longer to acquire)</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you spend XP every time you cast a rote that's not really comparable. The drawback of Devices is that they have to be recharged every so often with Quint or Tass - and if you run out of such, they stop working.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and that the Permadox/Genetic Flaws that Enhancements have come from them being an unnatural distortion of the subject's Pattern; Rotes aren't. </div> </div> </div>I'm looking at this from a game design perspective, not a lore one. From an OOG point of view, Permadox is intended to balance having a Device implanted that is extremely difficult to remove on account of it being literally part of your character's body. Genetic Flaws ... ugh. They don't seem to have much mechanical support, literally including things like &quot;is bald&quot; or &quot;talks quickly&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if you want to pick up on the \u201cRise of the Extraordinary Citizen\u201d metaplot idea introduced in the Revised NWO Convention Book (i.e., \u201cever since the Dimensional Anomaly rolled around, the number of Extraordinary Citizens has spiked; and nobody knows why\u201d), you're going to need something like what I'm describing.<br /> <br /> And as such, it wouldn't really be relevant to M5. For M5, I'd insist that Hedge Magic never even gets referenced; just use the \u201cMagic by Rote\u201d option to handle acolytes and extraordinary citizens who actually know a trick or two. </div> </div> </div>I'd be happy to use &quot;Magic by Rote&quot; to model the actions of sorcerers, but allowing PC mages to go above their sphere and Arete ratings seems to remove the point of Arete and Spheres.<br /> <br /> Also, HAP/PBD should be enshrined as the definitive way magic works. RBD and the like should be variant options located in the Storyteller's Guide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1403871#post1403871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> that could work,<br /> but how many in a large city like new york?</div> </div> </div> </div>Checking ... Vegas has 4 chantries, two Traditional and two Technocrat. For such a prominent and major city as NYC, I would double or even quadruple that, and add some various cabals or independent mages here and there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the thing with vampires is that their numbers tend to go over the 1 in 100 000<br /> <br /> in some city by night books, the named npcs go over the ratio </div> </div> </div>Well, it need not be taken as an exact measure of how many mages are active in the world. More a general guideline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 07-23-2020, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T21:00:43-07:00","id":1404352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1404326#post1404326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you spend XP every time you cast a rote that's not really comparable. The drawback of Devices is that they have to be recharged every so often with Quint or Tass - and if you run out of such, they stop working.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I misunderstood what you were saying; I thought you were talking about the Quintessence that goes into <i>creating</i> a Device or Talisman, not the Quintessence that's needed to <i>use</i> it. In that regard, I have no trouble whatsoever saying that each use of a Rote that's operating beyond your Spheres costs a point of Willpower. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1404326#post1404326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking at this from a game design perspective, not a lore one. From an OOG point of view, Permadox is intended to balance having a Device implanted that is extremely difficult to remove on account of it being literally part of your character's body. Genetic Flaws ... ugh. They don't seem to have much mechanical support, literally including things like &amp;quot;is bald&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;talks quickly&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Game design follows from lore; or at least it <i>should</i>. In this case, the reasoning behind the drawbacks of an Enhancement are a reflection of the fact that the character didn't develop the Enhancement's capabilities himself; so he has to pay some sort of price for taking a shortcut to power. Rotes, as I'm envisioning them, wouldn't be a shortcut: you spent the time and effort to learn them (as represented by the xp expenditure), so it's now a natural party of you rather than an invasive and decidedly unnatural alteration. Thus, no additional drawbacks beyond the aforementioned Willpower cost. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1404326#post1404326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be happy to use &amp;quot;Magic by Rote&amp;quot; to model the actions of sorcerers, but allowing PC mages to go above their sphere and Arete ratings seems to remove the point of Arete and Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two points here: <br /> <br /> First, it doesn't remove the point of Arete and Spheres at all, any more than Enhancements do. You're still better off in the long run developing your Arete and Spheres than relying on your Rotes; it's just that the Rotes give you a preview of what the Spheres are capable of. What the Spheres bring to the table that a collection of Rotes doesn't is versatility: each Rote lets you do <i>one thing</i>; what a dot in a Sphere lets you do is\u2026 well, very much <i>not</i> just one thing. <br /> <br /> Second: I'm not talking about <i>modeling sorcerers</i> using \u201cMagick by Rote\u201d; I'm talking about <i>presenting a separate kind of Sleeper magician</i> from Sorcerers and Hedge Magic, one that <i>literally is</i> a Sleeper using Awakened Magick in a limited way. I am <i>not</i> saying \u201cuse Magick by Rote if you don't have access to the Hedge Paths rules\u201d; I'm saying \u201cconsider using Magick by Rote <i>even if you do</i> have access to the Hedge Paths rules\u201d. <br /> <br /> And with that clarified (I hope), one of the differences between these \u201cRote-only mages\u201d and sorcerers is that these \u201crote magicians\u201d can't do anything that an Awakened Mage can't, while a sorcerer <i>can</i>. If a rote magician can perform an Effect that he has studied and mastered without having the Arete and Spheres that define an Effect, then an Awakened Mage should be able to put in the same time and effort to study and master an Effect without having the Arete and Spheres that define that Effect \u2014 though if he attempts to perform that Effect by Rote before he has developed his Spheres to the point that he doesn't need to do it by Rote, he has to labor under the same restrictions as the Rote Magician. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1404326#post1404326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, HAP/PBD should be enshrined as the definitive way magic works. RBD and the like should be variant options located in the Storyteller's Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a general rule of thumb, decisions should be made by the developers on each of the optional rules for Magick that appeared in M20, with the magick system in M5 either incorporating the rule as an integral part of the system or ignoring it; and the various optional rules that get left out of the core book could then appear in a supplement (such as an M5 Storyteller's Handbook). <br /> <br /> That said, one reason Brucato presented the notion of Subtle/Uncanny/Extreme in <b>Mage Made Easy</b> was an attempt to get around the whole \u201cHAB/HOO, RBD/PBD\u201d issue by shifting the decision to something easier to judge. I'm not sure he succeeded; but it was a valiant attempt, and I wouldn't mind if M5 were to try something similar. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1404326#post1404326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Checking ... Vegas has 4 chantries, two Traditional and two Technocrat. For such a prominent and major city as NYC, I would double or even quadruple that, and add some various cabals or independent mages here and there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, it need not be taken as an exact measure of how many mages are active in the world. More a general guideline.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMHO, <b>Ascension's Landscape</b> should be required reading for M5's developers. One thing that it points out is that depending on what canon source you cite and what method you use to determine how common active mages are, you could get an estimate of the mage population as high as 750,000 or as low as 1000.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T02:52:19-07:00","id":1404373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1404326#post1404326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it need not be taken as an exact measure of how many mages are active in the world. More a general guideline.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, I'm more curious about how the canon explains it,<br /> do people awaken more frequently?<br /> do they come from different areas and gather in one prominent city?<br /> the consequences of an influx in mages etc<br /> that sort of thing<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1404352#post1404352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMHO, <b>Ascension's Landscape</b> should be required reading for M5's developers. One thing that it points out is that depending on what canon source you cite and what method you use to determine how common active mages are, you could get an estimate of the mage population as high as 750,000 or as low as 1000.</div> </div> </div> </div>what's <b>Ascension's Landscape</b>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T05:26:34-07:00","id":1404385,"title":"","content":"It's a <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/299324\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Vault product</a> that takes a deep dive into issues of Mage world building. \u201cHow common are mages?\u201d is one of the topics it addresses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T06:22:59-07:00","id":1405320,"title":"","content":"Honestly now that I think about it, I really hope in M5 there will the Technocracy Civil War started because of Sars-Cov-2 because the NWO kept it under the cover because mayby it whas the Progenitors work or they thought it will so spread out and bring the people closer to technology spreading so the technocratic enlightment but now the Syndicate is very pissed because it fucked up really the market because scared people will not buy anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T14:51:20-07:00","id":1405406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1405320#post1405320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly now that I think about it, I really hope in M5 there will the Technocracy Civil War started because of Sars-Cov-2 because the NWO kept it under the cover because mayby it whas the Progenitors work or they thought it will so spread out and bring the people closer to technology spreading so the technocratic enlightment but now the Syndicate is very pissed because it fucked up really the market because scared people will not buy anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly disagree with this on two major points. First, we do not want a repeat of the stupidity of V5 controversy. Blaming an real world outbreak, one that's killed thousands and thousands of people worldwide and is currently still killing people is a <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><u><i><b>BAD</b></i></u></span> idea. Not to mention that it such an absurdly risky and stupid move that barring the individuals in question spending a ridiculous amount of time and effort keeping their superiors in the dark, they're going to get shut down. Look at the opening/closing fiction of the Rev Ed Syn CB. It's literally a Syndicate agent shutting down a Progenitor team's efforts to fast track a cure for cancer to the Sleepers because they're ignoring the dangers involved in rushing things to the Masses before they are ready for it.<br /> <br /> The idea of creating a virus to kill Sleepers and scare them into embracing technology and science is... well at best something the more one-dimensional evil depictions of the Union would do. And even then that borders on sheer insanity.<br /> <br /> Second, I frankly believe that they would never do a Union Civil War nor believe that they ever should. Now I should start first, that I'm not against them giving us the tools to enact such a conflict in our games but actually doing it in the canon would be a terrible move. First off there are only three real board outcomes they do with such a thing: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>One side wins the war and becomes the new Union</li> <li>The war becomes a stalemate and the Technocracy fractures in two</li> <li>The Technocracy collapses from the infighting into a diminished state</li> </ol><br /> With Option 1, whatever the outcome, you're going to annoy people as it takes away their options for using the Technocracy. Those that want the Technocracy to be nuanced and/or more morally centered or light is not going to like it if the darker side wins and we're only left with that aspect of the Technocracy and vice versa.<br /> <br /> While Option 2 would see those factions preserved, it would also undermine the threat of the Technocracy to outsiders like the Traditions and Crafts as suddenly the weakness of the Technocratic Monolith has not been laid bare for all to see but has seen it torn asunder. Suddenly the Union is no longer the top dog and while in-universe that would be great for the Traditions and Crafts, it would also mean that one of the core elements of MtAs is lost, the underdog struggle of the Traditions against the dominant Technocracy.<br /> <br /> And it's the same for Option 3 but potentially worse as it isn't mutually exclusive from the other two options.<br /> <br /> Second is the fact that such a war would not be clean divide in the Union along Convention lines despite what some would claim. Indeed, much of the fighting between the NWO and the Syn is more over who should be the First Among Equals thing going on between the two Conventions, their particular world views and general bitching about the screw ups of the other. As a result if outfighting did break out between them, it's unlikely that any of the other Conventions would fully support one side or the other. Hell if anything, ItX, Prog and VE are just as likely to band together and tell the NWO and Syn to knock it off. And given the military might of just the VE, that would likely see the conflict end right then and there.<br /> <br /> And that's kind of the thing, for all the talk of a Technocrat Civil War, unless circumstances drastically change, all it will ever be is just that, talk and the jockeying of power between the NWO and the Syn.<br /> <br /> Finally from an out-of-universe perspective, the Conventions work fine just as they are. Each cover their own sphere of sciences, technologies and politics, and each Convention provides valuable things for the others. Taking them apart upsets the balance within the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Frankly I hope the people that do work on M5 look to what's been done with the Union in recent years and use that as a springboard for them in M5. Keep them strong and unified to outsiders while inside they're struggling against themselves and their own flaws and failures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T17:22:28-07:00","id":1405422,"title":"","content":"What he said. The Technocratic civil war works best as a potential threat in the future which PCs' actions can ignite or prevent than as something that actually happens in the metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T18:05:23-07:00","id":1405433,"title":"","content":"\u2026unless, of course, you <i>want</i> some of the consequences that a \u201ccivil war\u201d may bring. <br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not so much for an all-out civil war (and certainly not the \u201cNWO vs. Syndicate\u201d notion that the Revised Convention Books were pushing) as I am for Navalon to become a thing: much like when the Electrode Engineers and Virtual Adepts left the Union, except this time it isn't a whole Convention that's leaving but rather members from all over the Union, and they're not interested in joining the Traditions and compromising their Enlightened Science. <br /> <br /> The key point to this is that the Technocracy survived two defections in the past; they can survive a third.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T12:42:46-07:00","id":1405653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1405433#post1405433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026unless, of course, you <i>want</i> some of the consequences that a \u201ccivil war\u201d may bring.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not so much for an all-out civil war (and certainly not the \u201cNWO vs. Syndicate\u201d notion that the Revised Convention Books were pushing) as I am for Navalon to become a thing: much like when the Electrode Engineers and Virtual Adepts left the Union, except this time it isn't a whole Convention that's leaving but rather members from all over the Union, and they're not interested in joining the Traditions and compromising their Enlightened Science.<br /> <br /> The key point to this is that the Technocracy survived two defections in the past; they can survive a third.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious, what is it you don't like about VAs that you want Navalon so badly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T17:39:48-07:00","id":1405702,"title":"","content":"It's not that I don't like them; it's that they don't do what I want from an \u201cEnlightened Scientists, but not Technocrats\u201d faction. They're too focused on Information, which is all well and good as far as it goes but doesn't go far enough; and their mindset is about as close to being mystical as you can get while still being on the technomancer side of the technomancer/mystic divide. And they've bought into the Traditions' shared worldview of \u201cWe're All Gods in Disguise\u201d and its variants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-31-2020, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T19:05:06-07:00","id":1405721,"title":"","content":"Honestly while I understand where you're coming from Data, I disagree on the VA and for that matter on the idea of Navalon breaking away from the Union and becoming it's own thing. With the former, the Traditions are designed to have an air of wonder and the fantastic to them. The VA are no different in that regard. They've always had that fantastical edge to them and their beliefs. Making them more... grounded for the lack of a better word like the Conventions would really make their existence as a Tradition weird. They would stick out like a sore thumb and beg the question of why they are a Tradition and not a Convention.<br /> <br /> With Navalon, it's kind of the same thing as even if they joined the Disparate Alliance they would still stick out from everyone else and I can't really see them as a real, viable option on their own short of a Major Technocrat Schism/Civil War which I've already said my dislike for that. Personally I much prefer Navalon as a political faction/conspiracy within the Union trying to keep them true to their more nobler origins. And as a Player and Storyteller, I see there being far more potential and options with that set up than making them their own thing divorced from the Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T21:22:31-07:00","id":1405743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1405721#post1405721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly while I understand where you're coming from Data, I disagree on the VA and for that matter on the idea of Navalon breaking away from the Union and becoming it's own thing. With the former, the Traditions are designed to have an air of wonder and the fantastic to them. The VA are no different in that regard. They've always had that fantastical edge to them and their beliefs. Making them more... grounded for the lack of a better word like the Conventions would really make their existence as a Tradition weird. They would stick out like a sore thumb and beg the question of why they are a Tradition and not a Convention.</div> </div> </div> </div>When did I say that I want to change the VAs in any way? I like them the way they are. They just don't fill the role that I want to see filled: Enlightened Scientists who aren't Technocrats. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1405721#post1405721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Navalon, it's kind of the same thing as even if they joined the Disparate Alliance they would still stick out from everyone else and I can't really see them as a real, viable option on their own short of a Major Technocrat Schism/Civil War which I've already said my dislike for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's where I differ: I <i>can</i> see them as a real, viable option on their own without a major Technocrat civil war; just a purge. Again, I point you to the defections of the Electrodyne Engineers and Virtual Adepts: if they could leave the Union and form viable Traditions, then the Harbingers of Avalon can leave the Union and form a viable Craft. Heck, even the Templar are an example of this, as that Craft is descended from the survivors of a Technocratic purge. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1405721#post1405721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I much prefer Navalon as a political faction/conspiracy within the Union trying to keep them true to their more nobler origins. And as a Player and Storyteller, I see there being far more potential and options with that set up than making them their own thing divorced from the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div> But we have the Cassandra Complex, the Friends of Courage, and Project Invictus for that kind of game. Conversely, making them their own thing divorced from the Technocracy opens up a play option that isn't really addressed right now: the aforementioned \u201cEnlightened Scientists who aren't Technocrats\u201d. And I find <i>that</i> option much more appealing than \u201cyet another dissident faction within the Technocracy\u201d. <br /> <br /> Mind you, I'm not against there being more dissident factions within the Union \u2014 though I'd be more inclined to evolve Project Invictus and broaden its goals from \u201cinvestigate SPD\u201d to \u201cinvestigate all sorts of Technocratic corruption\u201d: Autochthonia, SPD, Threat Null, Threat Negation, Fallen infiltration of the Void Engineers, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T04:05:28-07:00","id":1405776,"title":"","content":"As I said before, while the *idea* of Navalon might be good, the name isn't. It sounds more like a brand of prescription medicine than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T04:21:13-07:00","id":1405777,"title":"","content":"And to me, the name is the least important thing about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T04:57:24-07:00","id":1405779,"title":"","content":"From what I understood from Navalon is that they are closer to be Mages with Technic group or better said, that they would try to fuse technik and machines like for example in Knights and Magic whith an organization like Kingsman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T12:26:20-07:00","id":1405824,"title":"","content":"Not really, no. The Harbingers of Avalon are Enlightened Scientists just like any Technocrat, and their Practices work the same way that any Technocratic Practices work. Where the Harbingers differ from the rest of the Union (and why they're half a step away from cutting loose from the Union, according to M20) is in their Paradigm, the \u201cwhy do you do what you do, and what are you hoping to accomplish\u201d part of the Focus. The Harbingers believe that the Union has lost its way; and if they abandon the Union, it will be because they think that it's doing too much damage and that working within the system to fix it is too little, too late of a fix. Navalon will form if the Harbingers' leadership decides that they need the freedom to act openly against the Union's policies instead of being limited to efforts to quietly subvert the machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T14:26:45-07:00","id":1405831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1405776#post1405776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said before, while the *idea* of Navalon might be good, the name isn't. It sounds more like a brand of prescription medicine than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>petition to rename them to Data Weavers...actually, that sounds more like a name for virtual adepts :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T15:23:07-07:00","id":1405842,"title":"","content":"It still kills me that the virtual adepts aren't calling themselves Tech Wizards","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T15:47:33-07:00","id":1405846,"title":"","content":"If they have to rename the VAs, I'd prefer Tech Wizards to Mercurial Elite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T01:35:45-07:00","id":1405899,"title":"","content":"I prefer Mercurial Elite, but Tech Wizard is good too","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T12:49:50-07:00","id":1405981,"title":"","content":"Honestly with how in VA Revised they go all about they are Elite and everyone else are Lamers I kind of understood that they took the chance to annoy the Order of Hermes while rebranding themselves calling themselves the Elite Merkurs and so giving the statement, they are the better ones like Novas Troops and the rest of the Order are just the common mages that are better in mass than class like the Raynor's Raiders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T13:45:58-07:00","id":1405988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1405846#post1405846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they have to rename the VAs, I'd prefer Tech Wizards to Mercurial Elite.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer Digital Elite, since a core part of their identity is tied up with the Digital Web, which they either discovered or created.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T14:04:00-07:00","id":1405992,"title":"","content":"But a big bunch of them are into Trinary so I don't think that'll work for them. <br /> <br /> if this was a decade and a half ago I'd consider... brace for it... <br /> <br /> &quot;The Mage L33t&quot; or M4G3 L33T or something fucking stupid. Maybe they could call themselves the Toy Boys.... <br /> <br /> Tech wizards is pretty timeless. I dunno, maybe in 30 years or so the youngins won't have that in their language, but I think Tech Wizards would've worked since... the 80's right? All the way to now. So it's got staying power in a field where everything changes really fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T14:24:50-07:00","id":1405998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398959-thinking-about-m5?p=1405988#post1405988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd prefer Digital Elite, since a core part of their identity is tied up with the Digital Web, which they either discovered or created.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though Digital Elite would state, that they are Uber in the Cyberspace but in Meatspace like a crocodile on land. Mercurial Elite would be way more powerfull because many people would not have some weak bleach hikkimokori in front of their eyes while imagine but muscular agile champions that are the 501st Equivalent of a God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T05:06:34-07:00","id":1406089,"title":"","content":"You know how homosexuals used to use coded language to signal others whilst staying hidden? &quot;mercurial elite&quot; sounds like such slang for a trans person. It doesn't work. Great as his works are, I don't think the VA are trying to emulate Oscar Wilde, but rather establish themselves as the -in-the-now- Technological mages of the Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}